hadiths[527]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4628","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah created Adam in His image, his height was sixty cubits. When He created him, He said: Go and greet that group, a group of angels who were sitting, and listen carefully to the reply they give you, for that will be your greeting and the greeting of your descendants."" So he went and said to them: As-salamu Alaikum! They replied: As-salamu Alaika wa Rahmatullah! They added the words 'wa Rahmatullah' in their reply."" He said: ""Everyone who enters Paradise will be in the form of Adam, his height will be sixty cubits. After him, the creation has been decreasing in stature continuously up to now."" Agreed upon."
"4629","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Which (manners) of Islam are the best?"" He replied: ""(That) you feed (others), and you greet with peace both those whom you know and those whom you do not know."" Agreed upon."
"4630","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A believer has six rights over another believer: When he falls ill, visit him; when he dies, attend his funeral; when he invites you, accept his invitation; when you meet him, greet him with salam; when he sneezes (and says Alhamdulillah), respond to him by saying Yarhamuk Allah; and wish well for him in his presence and in his absence."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Nasa'i and al-Tirmidhi. The author of Mishkat says: And I have not found it in the Sahihayn nor in the book of al-Humaydi, but the author of Jami' al-Usul (Ibn al-Athir) has mentioned it from the narration of al-Nasa'i."
"4631","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You cannot enter Paradise until you become believers, and you cannot become believers until you love one another. Shall I not tell you about something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread peace among yourselves."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4632","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rider should greet the one who is walking, the one who is walking should greet the one who is sitting, and the smaller group should greet the larger group."" Agreed upon."
"4633","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The younger should greet the elder, the one who is walking should greet the one who is sitting, and the smaller group should greet the larger group."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4634","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some children and greeted them with salam. Agreed upon."
"4635","Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do not initiate the greeting of peace with the Jews and Christians, and when you meet any of them on the road, force them to the narrowest part of it."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4636","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When the Jews greet you, one of them says: 'As-Saam Alaik' (death be upon you), so you should reply to them: 'Wa Alaik' (and upon you)."" Agreed upon."
"4637","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the People of the Book greet you with Salam, then you should reply: 'Wa Alaikum.'"" Agreed upon."
"4638","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A group of Jews sought permission to meet the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and they said: “Death be upon you.” I said: “Rather, death and curse be upon you.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Aisha! Indeed, Allah is gentle and loves gentleness in every matter.” I said: “Did you not hear what they said?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I replied: ‘And upon you (death be upon you).’” And in another narration: the words are “upon you,” and they did not mention the conjunction “and.” And in the narration of Bukhari: Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “The Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ‘Death be upon you.’ The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ‘And upon you.’” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “Death be upon you, may Allah curse you, and may His anger be upon you.” (Upon hearing this) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Aisha! Hold back, be gentle, and avoid harshness and foul speech.” She said: “Did you not hear what they said?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Did you not hear what I said? I replied to them, and my supplication against them was accepted, while their supplication against me was not accepted.” And in the narration of Muslim: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not be abusive, for Allah does not like indecency or forced indecency.” Agreed upon."
"4639","It is narrated from Usama bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by a gathering in which Muslims, idol-worshipping polytheists, and Jews were sitting, so he, peace and blessings be upon him, greeted them with salam. Agreed upon."
"4640","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Avoid sitting on the roads."" The companions said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Sitting there is a necessity for us, we cannot do without it, we sit there and talk."" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you must sit, then give the road its due right."" They asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the right of the road?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Lowering the gaze, not causing harm, responding to greetings, enjoining good, and forbidding evil."" Agreed upon."
"4641","Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding the story mentioned in the previous hadith, that he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""And guiding the way."" Imam Abu Dawood has narrated in a similar manner after the hadith narrated from Abu Saeed Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him. Its chain is good; narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4642","Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding this incident, that he said: ""Help the oppressed and guide the one who has lost his way."" Imam Abu Dawood has narrated in a similar manner after the hadith of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, and I have not found these two hadiths in the Sahihain. Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4643","Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: ""A Muslim has six rights over another Muslim according to custom: When he meets him, he should greet him with salam; when he invites him, he should accept it; when he sneezes (and says 'Alhamdulillah'), he should say to him 'Yarhamuk Allah'; when he falls ill, he should visit him; when he dies, he should attend his funeral; and he should like for him what he likes for himself."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and al-Darimi."
"4644","It is narrated from Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""As-salamu Alaikum!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to him, then he sat down. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(For him) there are ten (good deeds)."" Then another person came and said: ""As-salamu Alaikum wa Rahmatullah!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to him, and when he sat down, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(For him) there are twenty (good deeds)."" Then another person came and said: ""As-salamu Alaikum wa Rahmatullahi wa Barakatuh!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to him, and when he sat down, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(For him) there are thirty (good deeds)."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4645","Mu’adh bin Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith of the same meaning, adding that then another man came and said: “As-salamu ‘alaykum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu wa maghfiratuhu!” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “(For him) there are forty (good deeds).” And he said: “Virtues are like this.” Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4646","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who initiates the greeting of peace is closest to Allah."" Sahih, narrated by Ahmad, al-Tirmidhi, and Abu Dawood."
"4647","It is narrated from Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some women and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted them with salam. Hasan, narrated by Ahmad."
"4648","Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When a group of people passes by, it is sufficient for one person among them to give the greeting (salaam), and for those who are sitting, it is sufficient for one person among them to reply. Baihaqi narrated it as marfu’ in Shu’ab al-Iman. And Abu Dawood, after narrating this hadith, said: Hasan bin Ali narrated it as marfu’, and he is a teacher of Abu Dawood. Hasan, narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman and Abu Dawood."
"4649","Amr bin Shu’aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever imitates anyone other than us is not from among us. Do not imitate the Jews and Christians, for the greeting of the Jews is to gesture with the fingers, while the greeting of the Christians is to gesture with the palms. (Tirmidhi), and he said: Its chain is weak. Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4650","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When any one of you meets his (Muslim) brother, he should greet him with Salam. If a tree, wall, or stone comes between them and then they meet again, he should greet him with Salam again."" Its chain is authentic, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4651","Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you enter a house, greet its inhabitants with salam, and when you leave, bid farewell to its inhabitants with salam."" Al-Bayhaqi has narrated it as a mursal hadith in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4652","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Son! When you go to your family, greet them with salam; (in this way) there will be blessings upon you and your household."" Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4653","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""First give salam, then speak."" Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is munkar. Its chain is very weak. Narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4654","Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In the days of ignorance, when we met (someone), we used to say: ""May Allah keep your eye cool, and may you wake up fresh and happy."" When Islam came, we were forbidden from this. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4655","Ghalib narrates: We were sitting at the door of Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) when a man came and said: My father narrated from my grandfather, who said: My father sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Go to him and convey my greetings. He said: I reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father sends you greetings. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Peace be upon you and your father."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4656","It is narrated from Abu Al-Ala bin Hadhrami that Alaa Hadhrami (may Allah be pleased with him) was the governor of Bahrain appointed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and when he wrote letters to you, he would begin with his own name (from Alaa). Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4657","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you writes a letter, let him dust it with earth, for by doing so the task is completed quickly and easily."" (Tirmidhi), and he said: This hadith is munkar. Its chain is very weak. Narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4658","Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was present in the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and there was a scribe before him. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Place the pen on your ear, for doing so (placing the pen on the ear) helps one remember the purpose and outcome quickly."" (Tirmidhi), and he said: This hadith is gharib and its chain is weak. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4659","Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed me to learn the Syriac language. In another narration, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said that I should learn the writing of the Jews, and he said: ""I fear for the writing of the Jews."" Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I learned their language in less than half a month. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote letters to the Jews, I would write them, and when they wrote letters to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I would read their letters to him. Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4660","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When any one of you comes to a gathering, he should greet (with salam), then if he wishes to sit, he may sit. And when he gets up to leave, he should greet (with salam). The first (greeting) does not have more right than the second (greeting)."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4661","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no good or benefit in sitting on the roads, except for the one who guides the way, responds to greetings, lowers his gaze, and helps in loading a burden onto a mount."" And the hadith narrated from Abu Jurayy is mentioned in the chapter ""The Virtue of Charity."" Its chain of narration is very weak; it is narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4662","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah created Adam (peace be upon him) and breathed the soul into him, he sneezed and said, 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is due to Allah). He praised Allah by Allah’s guidance, so his Lord said to him: 'May Allah have mercy on you, O Adam!' Go to that group of angels who are sitting and say to them: 'As-salamu alaikum!' So he went and said: 'As-salamu alaikum!' They replied: 'Wa alaikas-salam wa rahmatullah!' Then he returned to his Lord, who said: 'Indeed, this is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants among themselves.' Allah commanded him while both His hands were closed: 'Choose whichever you wish from among them.' He said: 'I have chosen the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are right and blessed.' Then Allah spread out His right hand, and in it were Adam and his descendants. He said: 'O Lord! Who are these?' He replied: 'These are your descendants. The lifespan of every human being was written between his eyes, and among them was a man who was the brightest of them (in face).' He said: 'O Lord! Who is this?' He replied: 'This is your son Dawud (David), and I have written his lifespan as forty years.' He said: 'O Lord! Increase his lifespan.' Allah said: 'This is what I have written for him.' He said: 'O Lord! I have given him sixty years from my own lifespan.' Allah said: 'This is your decision.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Then he remained in Paradise as long as Allah willed, then he was sent down from there, and Adam (peace be upon him) used to count his age. When the Angel of Death came to him, he said: 'You have come early, for my age was written as a thousand years.' He replied: 'Yes, but you gave sixty years to your son Dawud (David).' He denied it, and so his descendants also denied. And he forgot, so his descendants also forget.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'From that day, the command was given to write and to bear witness.'"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4663","Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a group of our women and greeted us with salam. Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood, Ibn Majah, and Al-Darimi."
"4664","It is narrated from Tufail bin Abi bin Ka'b that he used to come to Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he would go with him to the market in the morning. The narrator states: When we would go to the market, Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would greet everyone he passed by there—those engaged in small business, the wealthy, the poor, and anyone else. Tufail narrates: One day I came to Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he told me to go to the market. I said to him: What will you do in the market? You do not stop at any sale, nor do you inquire about any transaction, nor do you ask about prices, nor do you sit in the gatherings of the market. So please stay here and let us talk. The narrator states: Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: O man with a belly! The narrator states: Tufail had a large belly. We go for the purpose of greeting (saying salam); we greet everyone we meet. Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Malik and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4665","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""So-and-so has a date-palm tree in my garden, and because of this date-palm tree he causes me harm."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a message to him to sell his date-palm tree to me. He said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then give it to me as a gift."" He said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sell it to me in exchange for a date-palm tree in Paradise."" He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have not seen anyone more miserly than you, except one who is miserly in greeting with peace."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4666","Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who initiates the greeting of peace is free from arrogance."" Its chain is weak; it was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4667","Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us and said, ""Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) summoned me to him. I came to his door and greeted (with salam) three times. I did not receive a reply, so I returned. He (Umar) asked me: 'What prevented you from coming to us?' I said: 'I came and greeted at your door three times, but you did not reply, so I went back, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed me: ""When any of you seeks permission three times and is not granted permission, let him return.""' Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Present evidence for this.' Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'I stood with them and went to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and testified.' Agreed upon."
"4668","Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Your seeking permission from me is that you lift the curtain and listen to my private words (so come in), until I forbid you from doing so."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4669","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the debt owed by my father, and I knocked at the door. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who is it?"" I replied: ""It is I."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""'It is I, it is I.'"" As if he disliked this. Agreed upon."
"4670","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I entered the house with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he found some milk in a bowl. He said: ""Abu Hurairah! Go to the people of Suffah and bring them to me."" I went to them and called them. They came and sought permission (to enter), and he granted them permission, so they entered. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4671","It is narrated from Kaldah bin Hanbal that Safwan bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) sent (through my hand) milk or a fawn and a cucumber to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the upper area. The narrator states: I went to him but neither greeted nor sought permission. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Go back and say: As-salamu Alaikum! May I come in?"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4672","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any of you is invited and he comes along with the messenger who brought the invitation, then that is permission for him."" And in his narration, it is mentioned: ""A man sending a messenger to another man is itself permission."" Weak, narrated by Abu Dawood. Authentic, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4673","Abdullah bin Busr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would come to someone's door, he would not face his face directly towards the door, rather he would come to its right corner or left corner and would say: ""As-salamu Alaikum! As-salamu Alaikum!"" In those days, there were no curtains on the doors. Its chain of narration is Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood. And the hadith narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As-salamu Alaikum wa Rahmatullah"" is mentioned in the chapter of Hospitality."
"4674","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about a matter, saying: Should I seek permission from my mother (when going to her)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes."" The man said: I live with her in the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Still, seek her permission."" The man said: I am her servant. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Still, seek permission. Do you like to see her in a naked state?"" He said: No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then seek her permission."" Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated it as mursal. Its chain is weak, there is no risalah, narrated by Malik."
"4675","Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I had permission to visit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at night and during the day. When I would go at night, he (peace and blessings be upon him) would cough for me (as a sign of permission). Chain is weak, narrated by Al-Nasa'i."
"4676","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not grant permission to the one who does not begin with salam (greeting of peace) when seeking permission."" Its chain of narration is weak; it is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4677","Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: I asked Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Was there (the practice of) handshaking among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He replied: ""Yes."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4678","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) kissed Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). At that time, Aqra’ bin Habis (may Allah be pleased with him) was also present with him. Aqra’ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have ten children, and I have not kissed any of them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) looked at him (in astonishment), then said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.” Agreed upon. And the hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): ((A-thamma Luka‘)) will, insha’Allah, be mentioned in the chapter on the virtues of the Ahl al-Bayt of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family and upon them all). Whereas the hadith narrated from Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) has been mentioned in the chapter on protection."
"4679","Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When two Muslims meet and shake hands, they are forgiven before they part.” (Ahmad, Tirmidhi, Ibn Majah). And in the narration of Abu Dawood, it is stated: “When two Muslims meet and shake hands, praise Allah, and seek forgiveness from Him, they are forgiven.” Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad, Tirmidhi, Ibn Majah, and Abu Dawood."
"4680","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! When one of us meets his brother or his friend, should he bow his head before him?"" He replied, ""No."" He asked, ""Should he embrace him and kiss him?"" He replied, ""No."" He asked, ""Should he take his hand and shake hands with him?"" He replied, ""Yes."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4681","It is narrated from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Visiting a sick person is fulfilled in such a way that one of you places his hand on the patient’s forehead or on his hand and asks him: ‘How are you?’ And your complete greeting among yourselves is to exchange salutations and shake hands.” Ahmad, Tirmidhi, and Imam Tirmidhi (may Allah have mercy on him) declared it weak. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"4682","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Zaid bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Madinah while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was present in my house. He came to you and knocked on the door. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), out of intense love, went towards him dragging his garment, without wearing a shirt. By Allah! I had never seen you without a shirt before or after that. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) embraced him and kissed him. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4683","Ayub bin Basheer narrates from a man of the Anzah tribe that he said: I asked Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him): When you used to meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), did he use to shake hands with you? He replied: Whenever I met him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shook hands with me. One day he sent for me, but I was not at home. When I came, I was informed, so I presented myself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting on a bedstead. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced me; this (embrace) was very good, very good. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4684","Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The day I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to Islam, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Welcome to the emigrant rider."" Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4685","Usayd bin Hudayr (may Allah be pleased with him) belonged to a tribe of the Ansar. He narrates: One day he was talking to people and he had a humorous nature, and he was making them laugh with his words. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) poked him in the side with a stick. He said: Let me take retaliation. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take retaliation."" He said: You are wearing a shirt while I am not wearing a shirt. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted his shirt, so I embraced him and began to kiss his side, and said: O Messenger of Allah! This is all I wanted. Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4686","It is narrated from Sha’bi (may Allah have mercy on him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) welcomed Ja’far bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he embraced him and kissed him between his eyes (on his forehead). Abu Dawood, Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman (mursal). In some versions of Mishkat and in Sharh al-Sunnah, it is connected through the chain of al-Bayazi. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood and al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"4687","It is narrated from Ja'far bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the incident of returning from the land of Abyssinia, he said: When we reached Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) welcomed me and embraced me, then said: ""I do not know whether I am more pleased with the conquest of Khaybar or with the arrival of Ja'far."" Coincidentally, his arrival was on the day of the conquest of Khaybar. Weak, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4688","Zari’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, and he was among the delegation of Abdul Qais: When we reached Madinah, we hurriedly dismounted from our mounts and kissed the hands and feet of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Its chain is weak; narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4689","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I have not seen anyone more similar to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) in manner, character, and appearance—in one narration, in speech—than Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). When she would come to him, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) would stand up to welcome her, take her by the hand, kiss her (on the forehead), and seat her in his place. And when he (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) would go to her, she would also stand up to welcome him, take his hand, kiss him, and seat him in her place. Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4690","Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: (Upon returning from a certain expedition) I was the first to arrive in Madinah along with Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and his daughter Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was lying down and suffering from fever. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to her and said: “Beloved daughter! How are you?” And he kissed her on the cheek. Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4691","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a child was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) kissed him and said: ""Listen! These (children) are a cause of stinginess and cowardice, and indeed they are a gift from Allah, the Exalted."" Weak, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4692","Yala (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them) came running quickly towards the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) embraced both of them and said: ""Indeed, children are a cause of miserliness and cowardice."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad."
"4693","It is narrated from Ata Khurasani (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shake hands with one another, (for) rancor departs thereby. Give gifts to one another, love will develop among you and enmity and resentment will disappear."" Imam Malik narrated it as a mursal narration. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Malik."
"4694","Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever performs four rak‘ahs (units of prayer) of Duha prayer before midday, it is as if he has performed those rak‘ahs on the Night of Qadr. And when two Muslims shake hands, all their sins fall away.” Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu‘ab al-Iman."
"4695","Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: When Banu Qurayza agreed to accept the decision of Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, sent someone to him, and he was nearby. So he came riding on a donkey, and when he reached near the mosque, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to the Ansar: ""Stand up for your leader."" Agreed upon. And this hadith has already been mentioned in full in the chapter on the ruling of captives."
"4696","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""No man should make another man get up from his place so that he may sit there; rather, make room and accommodate each other."" Agreed upon."
"4697","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever gets up from his place and then returns to it, he has more right to that place."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4698","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: There was no person more beloved to the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), yet when they saw him, they would not stand up, because they knew that he (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked it. And he said: This hadith is Hasan Sahih. Sahih, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4699","Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever likes that people stand before him, then he should make his abode in the Hellfire."" Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4700","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out leaning on a staff, so we stood up for him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not stand up as the non-Arabs stand up for each other in veneration."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4701","Saeed bin Abul Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us regarding a testimony, so a man stood up for him out of respect. He refused to sit there and said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also forbade that a person should wipe his hand with the garment of another person which he has not put on him. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4702","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would sit, we would sit around him. Then when he would stand up and intended to return, he would take off his sandal or place something of his there, by which the companions would understand (that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would return), and they would remain sitting there. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4703","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""It is not permissible for a man to separate two people without their permission (and sit between them)."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4704","Amr bin Shu'aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do not sit between two people without their permission."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4705","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to sit with us in the mosque and converse with us, and when he would stand up, we would remain standing for a long time until we saw that he had entered the house of one of his noble wives. Its chain is weak; it was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4706","Wathilah bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved from his place for him. The man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! There is enough space."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is the right of a Muslim that when his brother sees him, he should move (a little) for him."" Imam Bayhaqi has mentioned both hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4707","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, sitting in the courtyard of the Ka'bah with his hands clasped around his knees. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4708","Ubadah bin Tameem narrates from his uncle, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lying on his back in the mosque, with one of his legs placed over the other. Agreed upon."
"4709","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a man from lying on his back with one leg placed over the other. Narrated by Muslim."
"4710","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should lie on his back and place one foot over the other."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4711","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Once a man, dressed in a suit, was walking arrogantly, and his soul had made him conceited. He was caused to sink into the earth, and he will continue descending in it until the Day of Resurrection."" Agreed upon."
"4712","Jabir bin Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, reclining on a cushion on his left side. Its chain is authentic; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4713","Abu Saeed Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would sit in the mosque, he would clasp his hands together. Weak chain, narrated by Razeen."
"4714","Qilah bint Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sitting in the mosque in the position of qurfusā’ (sitting on his feet with his arms wrapped around his shins). She says, when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a state of humility and submissiveness, I trembled out of fear. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4715","Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform the Fajr prayer, he would remain seated in his place, cross-legged, until the sun had risen well. Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4716","It is narrated from Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped at night, he would lie down on his right side, and when he camped shortly before morning, he would prop up his elbow and rest his head on his palm. Sahih, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4717","Someone from the family of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated that the bed of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was only as much as the cloth in which a deceased is placed in the grave, and the mosque (some said: prayer mat) was near his head. Its chain of narration is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4718","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man lying on his stomach in the mosque and said: ""Allah does not like this way of lying."" Its chain is Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4719","Ya’ish bin Tikhfah bin Qais Ghifari narrates from his father, who was among the people of Suffah. He said: I was lying on my stomach due to pain in my chest when suddenly a man began nudging me with his foot and said: “Allah is displeased with lying in this manner.” I looked and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Ibn Majah."
"4720","Ali bin Shiban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps at night on the roof of a house without any barrier (on the roof), and in another narration: without stones on it, then the responsibility (of protection) has been lifted from him."" Abu Dawood and Ma'alim as-Sunan by Al-Khattabi contain the wording ((Hajji)). Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4721","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a person from sleeping on a roof that has no barrier. Its chain is weak; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4722","Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: Whoever sits in the middle of a gathering is cursed on the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4723","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The best gathering is the one which is spacious."" (Where people do not feel cramped while sitting.) Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4724","Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came and his noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) were sitting. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the reason that I see you sitting separately?"" Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4725","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any one of you is in the shade, then the (shade) moves away from him and part of his body is in the sun and part in the shade, then he should get up (from there)."" Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4726","In Sharh al-Sunnah, it is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you is in the shade and the shade moves away from him, then that person should get up (from there), because that is the gathering place of the devil."" Mu'ammar narrated it in the same way as a mawquf narration. Its chain is weak. Narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4727","It is narrated from Abu Saeed Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying as he was coming out of the mosque, and on the way men mixed with women. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to the women: ""Walk on the side of the road, you have no right to walk in the middle of the road, therefore walk on the edges of the road."" So (upon hearing this command) the woman would walk so close to the wall that her garment would cling to the wall. Its chain of narration is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4728","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade a man from walking between two women. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4729","Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: When we would present ourselves before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each one of us would sit wherever he found a place. Chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood. And two hadiths narrated from Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) have been mentioned in the chapter on Standing, and two hadiths narrated from Ali and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them) we will mention, if Allah wills, in the chapter on the Names and Attributes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4730","Amr bin Shuraid narrates from his father, who said: I was sitting in such a way that I had placed my left hand behind my back and was leaning on the flesh at the base of the thumb of my right hand. In this state, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by me and said: ""Do you sit like those upon whom wrath has been brought down (i.e., the Jews)?"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4731","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was lying on my stomach. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nudged me with his foot and said: ""Jundub! This is the way the people of Hell lie."" Sahih, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"4732","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Indeed, Allah likes sneezing and dislikes yawning. When one of you sneezes and says 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is due to Allah), it is obligatory upon every Muslim who hears him to say to him 'Yarhamukallah' (May Allah have mercy on you). As for yawning, it is from the devil; when one of you yawns, he should try his best to restrain it, for when one of you yawns, the devil laughs at him."" (Bukhari) And in the narration of Sahih Muslim: ""Because when one of you makes a sound while yawning, the devil laughs at him."" Narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"4733","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you sneezes, he should say 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is due to Allah), and his (Muslim) brother or companion should say to him 'Yarhamukallah' (May Allah have mercy on you). When he says to him 'Yarhamukallah', then (the one who sneezed) should say: 'May Allah guide you and set your condition right.'"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4734","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He responded to the sneeze of one of them but did not say anything to the other. The latter said, ""O Messenger of Allah! You prayed for him but did not pray for me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Because he said 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is due to Allah), but you did not say 'Alhamdulillah'."" Agreed upon."
"4735","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""When one of you sneezes and says 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is due to Allah), then you should supplicate for him. But if he does not say 'Alhamdulillah', then do not supplicate for him."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4736","It is narrated from Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man sneezed in his presence, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: “May Allah have mercy on you.” Then the man sneezed a second time, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The man has a cold.” And in the narration of Tirmidhi, when he sneezed a third time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “He has a cold.” Narrated by Muslim and Tirmidhi."
"4737","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When one of you yawns, he should place his hand over his mouth, for the devil enters (into the mouth)."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4738","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sneezed, he would cover his face with his hand or his garment, and with that he would lower his voice. Tirmidhi, Abu Dawood, and Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is Hasan Sahih. Its chain is Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4739","It is narrated from Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sneezes, he should say: All praise is due to Allah in every circumstance. And whoever responds to him should say: May Allah have mercy on you. And he (the one who sneezed) should say: May Allah guide you and rectify your condition."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and al-Darimi."
"4740","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Jews used to sneeze in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hoping that he would say to them, ""May Allah have mercy on you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""May Allah guide you and set your affairs right."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4741","Hilal bin Yasaf narrates: We were with Salim bin Ubaid when a man from among the people sneezed and said: ""As-salamu alaikum!"" (Upon hearing this) Salim said: ""Upon you and your mother."" It seemed that the man felt some displeasure in his heart. He (Salim) said: ""Listen! I have only said to you what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."" (Once) a man sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""As-salamu alaikum!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Upon you and your mother."" (Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) ""When one of you sneezes, he should say: ((Alhamdulillahi Rabbil 'Alamin)), and whoever responds to him should say: ((Yarhamukallah)), and then he should say: May Allah forgive me and you."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4742","Ubaid bin Rifa’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Respond with a supplicatory reply to the one who sneezes three times. If he sneezes more than that, then if you wish, reply to him, and if you wish, do not reply.” Abu Dawood, Tirmidhi, and they said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Tirmidhi."
"4743","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: ""Say the supplicatory response to your (Muslim) brother (in reply to his sneeze) three times; if the sneezing increases, then it is a cold."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood. And (the narrator) Sa‘id al-Maqburi said: I only know about him that he attributed the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as marfu‘."
"4744","It is narrated from Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) that a man sneezed beside Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: ""All praise is for Allah, and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."" (Upon hearing this) Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I also say: All praise is for Allah, and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. But saying it in this way is not established. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, taught us to say: All praise is due to Allah in every circumstance. (Reported by) Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4745","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughing so heartily that I could see the uvula of his throat; he would only smile. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4746","Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Since I accepted Islam, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prevented me (from attending his gatherings), and whenever he saw me, he smiled. Agreed upon."
"4747","Jabir bin Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would not rise from the place where he had performed prayer until the sun had risen. And when the sun had risen, he would stand up, and (during this time) the noble Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, would converse and discuss matters from the days of ignorance and would laugh, while the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, would only smile. And in the narration of Tirmidhi: they would recite poetry. Narrated by Muslim and Tirmidhi."
"4748","Abdullah bin Harith bin Jaz’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I have not seen anyone smile more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4749","Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked: Did the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) use to laugh? He replied: Yes! And the faith in their hearts was greater than a mountain. And Bilal bin Sa’d (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: They used to practice archery and would laugh looking at each other, and when night fell, they would become monks (i.e., ascetics), engaging in the worship of Allah. Weak, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4750","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the market when a man called out, ""Abul Qasim!"" When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned towards him, the man said, ""I was calling him (someone else)."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah."" Agreed upon."
"4751","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Name yourselves after me, but do not take my kunyah, for I have been made the Qasim (the distributor); I distribute among you."" Agreed upon."
"4752","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of your names, Abdullah and Abdur Rahman are the most beloved to Allah."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4753","Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not name your slave (child or slave) Yasar (Ease), Rabah (Profit), Najeeh (Successful), and Aflah (Prosperous), because you will say: 'Is he here?' If he is not there, then the one asking will say: 'He is not here.'"" And in his narration, it is mentioned: He said, ""Do not name your slave Rabah, Yasar, Aflah, and Nafi’."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4754","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to prohibit naming with names such as Ya'la, Barakah (Blessing), Aflah, Yasar, Nafi', and similar names. Then I saw that later he remained silent about it, and then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and did not prohibit it. Narrated by Muslim."
"4755","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the most detestable name in the sight of Allah will be that of a person who is called 'Shahanshah' (King of Kings)."" (Bukhari) And in the narration of Muslim, it is stated: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the person who will be most anger-provoking and have the most wicked name in the sight of Allah will be the one whose name is 'Shahanshah,' whereas only Allah is the Shahanshah."" (Agreed upon)"
"4756","Zainab bint Abi Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: My name was kept as Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not praise yourselves; Allah knows best who among you is righteous. Name her Zainab."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4757","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The name of Juwayriyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, was Barrah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, changed her name to Juwayriyyah, and he, peace and blessings be upon him, disliked that it be said: ""He has left from Barrah."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4758","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that a daughter of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was called Asiyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed her name to Jameelah. Narrated by Muslim."
"4759","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When Mundhir bin Abi Usaid was born, he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed him on his thigh and asked, “What is his name?” He said: So-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “No, rather his name is Mundhir.” Agreed upon."
"4760","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should say: 'My slave (male), my slave-girl (female),' for all of you are slaves and servants of Allah, and all your women are slave-girls of Allah. Rather, you should say: 'My boy, my girl.' And a slave should not say: 'My Lord!' Rather, he should say: 'My master.'"" In another narration: He should say: 'My chief, my patron.'"" In another narration: ""A slave should not say to his master: 'My patron,' for your patron is Allah."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4761","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Do not call (grapes) 'karm', for 'karm' is the heart of the believer."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4762","And in the hadith narrated by Wa'il bin Hujr (may Allah be pleased with him) in Muslim, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not say 'Karam', rather say 'Inab' and 'Habla' (grape)."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4763","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not call grapes 'Karam' and do not speak ill of time, for Allah Himself is time."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4764","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should speak ill of time, for Allah Himself is time."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4765","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say: My soul (self) has become impure, rather he should say: My soul has become heavy."" Agreed upon. And the hadith narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): ""The son of Adam hurts Me."" has already been mentioned in the chapter of faith."
"4766","Shuraih bin Hani narrates from his father that when he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with his people, he heard them calling his father by the nickname Abu al-Hakam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called him and said: ""Indeed, Allah is the Judge, and judgment belongs only to Him. Why have you been given the nickname Abu al-Hakam?"" He said: ""When my people differ over something, they come to me, and I judge between them, and both parties are satisfied with my decision."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How good this is. How many children do you have?"" He said: ""Shuraih, Muslim, and Abdullah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Which of them is the eldest?"" The narrator says: I said: ""Shuraih."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are Abu Shuraih."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood and al-Nasa'i."
"4767","Masruq narrates: I met Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: Who are you? I said: Masruq bin Ajda’. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Ajda’, is (the name of) a devil."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Ibn Majah."
"4768","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, you will be called by your names and the names of your fathers, so keep good names."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood."
"4769","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade that anyone should combine his name and his kunyah in such a way as to name himself Muhammad Abu al-Qasim. Sahih, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4770","It is narrated from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When you name (someone) with my name, then do not use my kunyah (patronymic) as a kunyah."" And Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is gharib, and in the narration of Abu Dawood, it is stated: ""Whoever names (someone) with my name should not use my kunyah, and whoever uses my kunyah should not name (someone) with my name."" Sahih, narrated by Tirmidhi, Ibn Majah, and Abu Dawood."
"4771","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah! A child has been born to me and I have named him Muhammad and given him the kunyah Abu al-Qasim, but I have heard that you dislike this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who is it that has made my name lawful and my kunyah unlawful, or who is it that has made my kunyah unlawful and my name lawful?"" Abu Dawood, and Muhyi al-Sunnah (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4772","Muhammad bin Hanafiyyah narrates from his father, who said: I asked, O Messenger of Allah! Tell me, if a child is born to me after you, may I name him after you and give him your kunyah? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4773","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I used to pick a herb, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave me the kunyah (Abu Hamzah) because of it. This was narrated by Tirmidhi, and he said: We know this hadith only through this route, and in Misbah it is stated that he declared it authentic. Its chain is very weak. Narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4774","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to change bad names. Sahih, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4775","Bashir bin Maimoon narrates from his uncle Usama bin Akhdari that a man named Asram was among those who came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, asked: ""What is your name?"" He replied: Asram. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""No, rather you are Zar'ah."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4776","And Abu Dawood said, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) changed the names ‘Aas, ‘Azeez, ‘Atlah, Shaytaan, Hakam, Ghuraab, Hubab, and Shihab, and he said: I have not mentioned their chains of narration for the sake of brevity. Authentic, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4777","It is narrated from Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), that either he said to Abu Abdullah or Abu Abdullah said to Abu Mas’ud: What have you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about the word “za’amu” (they claim)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “It is bad for a man to speak in such a manner.” Abu Dawood, and he said: By Abu Abdullah is meant Hudhaifah. Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4778","Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say: 'Whatever Allah wills and so-and-so wills,' but rather say: 'Whatever Allah wills, then so-and-so wills.'"" Its chain is authentic; narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood."
"4779","And in a disconnected narration, it is stated: ""Do not say: Whatever Allah wills and whatever Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) wills, but rather say: Whatever Allah alone wills."" Hasan, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4780","Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not call a hypocrite 'Sayyid' (master), because if he is a Sayyid (leader, master), then you have angered your Lord."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4781","Abdul Hameed bin Jubair bin Shaibah narrates: I was sitting with Saeed bin Musayyib when he related a hadith to me that his grandfather, Hazn, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""What is your name?"" He replied, ""My name is Hazn."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""(No), rather you are Sahl."" He said, ""I will not change the name given by my father."" Ibn Musayyib said: After that, harshness (huzoonat) remained among us. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4782","Abu Wahb al-Jushami reports: He said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Name yourselves after the names of the Prophets. The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah and Abdur Rahman. The truest names are Harith and Hammam, while the most detestable names are Harb and Murrah."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4783","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Two men came from the east and addressed (the people). The people were amazed at their speech, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some speech has the effect of magic."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4784","Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4785","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who speak with affectation have perished."" He said this three times. Narrated by Muslim."
"4786","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most truthful statement ever uttered by a poet is the saying of Labid: Behold! Everything except Allah is perishable."" Agreed upon."
"4787","Amr bin Shuraid narrates from his father, who said: One day I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you remember any poetry of Umayyah bin Abi Salt?"" I replied: Yes! He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite it!"" I recited a verse to him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite more!"" Then I recited another verse to him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite more!"" Until I had recited one hundred verses to him. Narrated by Muslim."
"4788","It is narrated from Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was participating in a battle when blood started to flow from his finger. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is only a finger that has bled, and whatever pain you have suffered is in the way of Allah."" Agreed upon."
"4789","Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the day of (the siege of) Banu Qurayzah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him): “Satirize the polytheists, Allah (and His help) is with you.” And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying to Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him): “Respond on my behalf, O Allah! Help him through Jibreel (peace be upon him).” Agreed upon."
"4790","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Satirize the Quraysh, for it is more severe upon them than shooting arrows at them."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4791","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say to Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him): ""As long as you satirize the polytheists in defense of Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him), Gabriel (peace be upon him) continues to assist you."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Hassan satirized them and brought comfort to the Muslims and found comfort himself."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4792","Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was carrying earth on the day of the Trench until his stomach was covered with dust. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was reciting (poetry): “By Allah! If Allah had not guided us, we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. So send down tranquility upon us, and make our feet firm when we meet (the enemies), for indeed they have transgressed against us. When they sought to cause us discord, we refused, we refused.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would raise his voice at the words: “We refused, we refused.” Agreed upon."
"4793","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Muhajirun and Ansar (may Allah be pleased with them) were digging the trench, carrying the earth, and saying: ""We are those who have pledged allegiance to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for jihad as long as we live."" In response, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying: ""O Allah! True life is the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun."" Agreed upon."
"4794","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is better for a man's belly to be filled with pus that corrodes it than to fill his belly with (blameworthy) poetry."" Agreed upon."
"4795","It is narrated from Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah Almighty has revealed a command regarding the condemnation of poetry. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! (This satire is such) as if you are shooting arrows at them."" In Al-Isti'ab by Ibn Abd al-Barr, it is mentioned that he said: O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about poetry? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the believer strives with his sword and his tongue."" Its chain is authentic, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4796","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Modesty and speaking little are branches of faith, while obscene speech and exaggeration are two branches of hypocrisy."" Its chain is authentic, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4797","It is narrated from Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, the one among you who is dearest and most beloved to me in this world, and the one who will be closest to me on the Day of Resurrection, is the one among you who has the best character. And the one among you who is most disliked by me in this world, and the one who will be farthest from me on the Day of Resurrection, is the one among you who has bad character, is excessively talkative, speaks rudely, and shouts when speaking.” Hasan, narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"4798","Imam Tirmidhi narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) in a similar manner. In his narration, it is mentioned that the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: O Messenger of Allah! We know about the talkative and the outspoken person, but who are meant by ""al-mutafayhiqoon""? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The arrogant ones."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4799","Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The Hour will not be established until a people will appear who will eat with their tongues (by flattering and earning wealth) just as a cow eats with its tongue.” Its chain is weak, narrated by Ahmad."
"4800","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah is hostile to the eloquent, exaggerated speaker who lives off his tongue, just as a cow eats with its tongue."" (Tirmidhi, Abu Dawood) And Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is hasan. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4801","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night of Mi'raj, I passed by some people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I asked: 'O Jibreel! Who are these people?' He replied: 'These are the preachers of your Ummah whose words and actions were contradictory.'"" (Tirmidhi), and he said: This hadith is gharib. Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4802","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever learns speech only so that he may, through it, gain control over the hearts of men or people, then on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will not accept any voluntary or obligatory act of worship from him."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4803","It is narrated from Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) that one day he said: A man stood up and, in order to display eloquence, prolonged his speech. So Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If he had adopted moderation while speaking, it would have been better for him, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""I have realized, or I have been commanded, to be concise in speech, for conciseness is better."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4804","Sakhr bin Abdullah bin Buraidah narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed, some speech has an effect like magic, some knowledge is ignorance, some poetry is wisdom, and some statements are burdens."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4805","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had a pulpit placed in the mosque for Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him). He would stand on it and boast on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) or defend him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: ""Indeed, Allah supports Hassan through Gabriel (peace be upon him) as long as he defends or boasts on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Bukhari in mu'allaq form."
"4806","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: There was a person who used to sing the camel songs for you; he was known by the name Anjasha, and he had a very beautiful voice. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Anjasha! Go slow, go slow, do not break the glass vessels."" Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He said this considering the delicacy of the women. Agreed upon."
"4807","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Poetry was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is a form of speech; whatever is good from it is good, and whatever is bad from it is bad."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Daraqutni."
"4808","Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated it as mursal from Urwah. Its chain of narration is very weak. Narrated by Al-Shafi'i."
"4809","Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: We were traveling with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, in (the region of Yemen) 'Arj when a poet appeared before us and began reciting poetry. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Seize this devil,"" or he said: ""Stop this devil (from reciting poetry), for it is better for a man's belly to be filled with pus than to be filled with poetry."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4810","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Singing creates hypocrisy in the heart just as water makes crops grow."" Its chain of narration is weak; it was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4811","Nafi’ reports: I was with Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) on a certain road when he heard the sound of a flute. He put his fingers into both his ears and moved off to the side of the road. After going some distance, he said to me: “Nafi’! Are you hearing anything now?” I said, “No.” He then removed his fingers from his ears and said: “I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he heard the sound of a flute, so he did just as I have done.” Nafi’ said: At that time, I was young. Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood."
"4812","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever guarantees me (the protection of) what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I guarantee him Paradise.” Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4813","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant utters a word that pleases Allah, and he gives it no importance, but because of it Allah raises him in degrees. And a servant utters a word that angers Allah, and he gives it no importance, but because of it he falls into Hell."" These are the words of Bukhari. And in the narration of Bukhari and Muslim: ""Because of it, he falls into Hell as deep as the distance between the east and the west."" __QUR_N__, __XREF_N__, __REF_N__"
"4814","Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abusing a Muslim is wickedness and fighting with him is disbelief."" Agreed upon."
"4815","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If a person says to his (Muslim) brother: 'Disbeliever,' then surely one of them will return to disbelief (from faith)."" Agreed upon."
"4816","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a person calls another person a fasiq (evildoer) or a kafir (disbeliever), and if the one who is being called is not such, then that (statement) returns upon the one who said it."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4817","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever calls someone a disbeliever or says: 'Enemy of Allah!' while he is not so, then that statement returns upon the one who said it."" Agreed upon."
"4818","It is narrated from Anas and Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Of two people who abuse each other, the sinner is the one who starts it, as long as the oppressed does not retaliate with more than one insult for one."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4819","It is narrated from Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is not appropriate for a truthful person to be excessively cursing."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4820","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Those who frequently curse will neither be witnesses nor intercessors on the Day of Resurrection."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4821","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a man says: The people have perished (because of their evil deeds), then he is the most perished among them all."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4822","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, you will find the worst person to be the one who is two-faced, who goes to some people with one story and to others with another story."" Agreed upon."
"4823","Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The tale-bearer will not enter Paradise."" And in the narration of Muslim, the word used is Nammam (""tale-bearer""). Agreed upon."
"4824","Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Adopt truthfulness, for truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues to speak the truth and seeks truthfulness until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful one (Siddiq). And beware of lying, for lying leads to sin, and sin leads to the Fire. A man continues to lie and seeks falsehood until he is recorded with Allah as a liar.” And in the narration of Muslim, he said: “Indeed, truthfulness is righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. And indeed, lying is sin, and sin leads to the Fire.” Agreed upon."
"4825","Umm Kulthum (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The person who reconciles between people is not a liar; he speaks good and conveys good."" Agreed upon."
"4826","Miqdad bin Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see those who excessively praise others, throw dust on their faces."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4827","Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man praised another man in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Woe to you! You have cut your brother's neck."" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this three times. ""If someone must praise, then let him say: I consider so-and-so to be such-and-such, while Allah knows best about his reality. If the person is as he thinks, then he should not declare anyone's purity before Allah with certainty."" Agreed upon."
"4828","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do you know what backbiting is?"" The noble companions, may Allah be pleased with them, said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is your mentioning about your brother something which he dislikes."" It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if what I say is actually present in my brother?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If what you say is in him, then you have backbitten him, and if what you say is not in him, then you have slandered him."" In another narration: ""When you say something about your brother which is in him, then you have backbitten him, and when you say something which is not in him, then you have slandered him."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4829","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Give him permission to enter, for he is a bad man of his people."" When he sat down, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed happiness on his face and smiled at him. When the man left, Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! You said such and such about him, then (when he came) you showed happiness on your face and smiled at him."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When did you ever find me to be foul-mouthed? For on the Day of Resurrection, the worst in status before Allah will be the one whom people leave alone to avoid his evil."" In another narration: ""To avoid his foul speech."" Agreed upon."
"4830","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""All the sins of my Ummah are forgivable except those who commit sins openly. And committing sins openly is that a person does an act (of sin) at night, then in the morning he goes around saying: O so-and-so! I did such and such last night, even though Allah had concealed it for him, and he spent the night while his Lord had covered him, but when morning comes, he removes Allah's covering from himself."" Agreed upon. And the hadith narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Whoever believes in Allah..."" is mentioned in the chapter of Hospitality."
"4831","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives up lying, even though he was in the wrong, a house will be built for him on the edge of Paradise. And whoever abandons arguing while being in the right, a house will be built for him in the middle of Paradise. And whoever improves his character, a house will be built for him in the highest part of Paradise."" Imam Tirmidhi has narrated this hadith and called it Hasan, and likewise it is in Sharh al-Sunnah and Misbahih, he said: This hadith is Gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4832","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what thing will cause most people to enter Paradise?"" (Then he said:) ""The fear of Allah and good character. Do you know what thing will cause most people to enter Hell?"" (Then he said:) ""Two things: the mouth and the private parts."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."
"4833","Bilal bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person utters a good word and he does not realize its significance, yet because of it Allah writes His pleasure for him until the Day of Resurrection. And indeed, a person utters a bad word and he does not realize its importance, so because of it Allah writes His displeasure for him until the Day of Resurrection."" Sharh al-Sunnah. And Imam Malik, Tirmidhi, and Ibn Majah have narrated a similar report. Its chain is Hasan. Narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah, Malik, Tirmidhi, and Ibn Majah."
"4834","Bahz bin Hakim narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Woe to the person who lies while speaking in order to make people laugh; woe to him, woe to him."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad, al-Tirmidhi, Abu Dawood, and al-Darimi."
"4835","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant speaks merely to make people laugh, and because of that he falls into Hell farther than the distance between the earth and the sky. And he does not slip as much by the slipping of his feet as he slips by the slipping of his tongue."" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4836","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever remains silent has attained salvation."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Ahmad, al-Tirmidhi, al-Darimi, and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4837","Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I asked, ""What is the means of salvation?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Control your tongue, let your house be sufficient for you, and weep over your sins."" Weak, narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"4838","Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith as marfu‘, he said: ""When the son of Adam wakes up in the morning, all the limbs beseech the tongue, saying: 'Fear Allah regarding us (in the matter of protecting our rights), for we are dependent on you; if you are upright, we will also be upright, and if you are crooked, we will also become crooked.'"" Its chain is good; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4839","Ali bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is from the excellence of a man's Islam that he leaves what does not concern him."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Malik and Ahmad."
"4840","Imam Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him. Its chain is weak, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"4841","Imam Tirmidhi and Bayhaqi have narrated it in Shu'ab al-Iman from both of them (Ali bin Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, and Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him). Its chain is weak. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4842","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One of the companions (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, so a man said: ""Glad tidings of Paradise to him."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know? Perhaps he spoke about something that did not concern him, or he was stingy with something that would not have decreased him."" Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4843","Sufyan bin Abdullah Thaqafi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you fear most for me?"" The narrator states: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held his tongue and said, ""This."" (Tirmidhi, and he declared it authentic.) Authentic, narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4844","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When a servant tells a lie, because of its stench, the angel moves a mile away from him."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4845","Sufyan bin Asad Hazrami (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The greatest betrayal is that you speak to your (Muslim) brother, and he believes you to be truthful, while you are lying to him."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4846","Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is two-faced in this world, on the Day of Resurrection his tongue will be of fire."" Hasan, narrated by al-Darimi."
"4847","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is neither one who taunts nor one who curses, nor is he indecent in speech nor abusive."" (Tirmidhi, Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman.) And in another narration of Bayhaqi: ""He is neither one who uses obscene language nor one who is abusive."" Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is gharib. Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4848","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A believer is not one who curses."" In another narration: ""It is not appropriate for a believer to be one who curses."" Its chain is good; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4849","Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say to one another: 'May Allah's curse be upon you,' 'May Allah's wrath be upon you,' or 'Go to Hell.'"" And in another narration: ""Do not even say: 'Go into the (Hell) Fire.'"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4850","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When a servant sends a curse upon something, the curse rises towards the sky, but before it reaches, the gates of the sky are closed. Then it descends towards the earth, and its gates are also closed. Then it turns to the right and to the left, and when it finds no way, it returns to the one upon whom the curse was sent, provided he is deserving of it; otherwise, it returns to the one who uttered it."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4851","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the wind blew away a man's sheet, so he cursed it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not curse it, for it is only following orders. And whoever sends a curse upon something that does not deserve it, the curse returns upon him."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4852","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let none of my companions convey to me anything (displeasing) about another companion, for I like that when I come to you, my heart is clean."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4853","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""It is enough for you regarding Safiyyah (peace and blessings be upon her) that she is such and such,"" meaning that she is short in stature. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have uttered a word which, if mixed with the sea, would overwhelm it (i.e., it would change its nature)."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Ahmad, al-Tirmidhi, and Abu Dawood."
"4854","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Obscenity in anything makes it defective, and modesty in anything adorns it."" Its chain is authentic, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4855","Khalid bin Ma'dan narrates from Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever reproaches his (Muslim) brother for a (past) sin, then this person will commit that (sin) before he dies."" This refers to the sin from which he has already repented. (Tirmidhi) And he said: This hadith is gharib, its chain is not connected because Khalid did not meet Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him). Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4856","Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not express joy at your (Muslim) brother's affliction, for it is possible that Allah may have mercy on him and test you with that (affliction)."" Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is Hasan Gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4857","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not like to imitate anyone, even if I were given such and such wealth."" Tirmidhi has narrated it and declared it authentic. Its chain is authentic, narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4858","Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A Bedouin came, made his camel sit down, tied it, and entered the mosque. He prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When the Prophet finished the prayer with salam, the Bedouin went to his mount, untied it, mounted it, and called out in a loud voice: “O Allah! Have mercy on me and on Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and do not include anyone else in our mercy.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do you think he is more ignorant, or his camel? Did you not hear what he said?” The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: Yes, we heard it. Its chain of narration is weak; it is narrated by Abu Dawood. And the hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): “It is enough for a man to be considered a liar that he narrates everything he hears.” This has already been mentioned in the first section of the chapter on holding fast (to the Book and Sunnah)."
"4859","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a sinner is praised, the Lord Almighty becomes displeased, and because of this (praise), His Throne trembles."" Its chain of narration is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4860","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer cannot be habitual of betrayal and lying; however, anything besides these can occur in him."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad."
"4861","Imam Bayhaqi narrated from Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) in Shu’ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"4862","It is narrated from Safwan bin Sulaim (may Allah have mercy on him) that it was asked from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Can a believer be a coward?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Yes."" Then it was asked: ""Can a believer be miserly?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Yes."" Then it was asked: ""Can a believer be a liar?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""No."" Malik and Bayhaqi have narrated it as mursal in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Malik and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4863","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Satan comes to people in human form, tells them false things, and then when the people disperse, one of them says: I heard a man. I recognize his face but I do not know his name; he was narrating this. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"4864","Imran bin Hattan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: I came to Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) and found him alone in the mosque, wrapped in a black cloak with a border. I said to him, ""Abu Dharr! Why this solitude?"" He replied, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Solitude is better than a bad companion, and a good companion is better than solitude. Writing a good word is better than silence, while silence is better than writing a bad word.'"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4865","It is narrated from Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man's maintaining silence (from saying bad things) is better than sixty years of worship."" Its chain is weak; it was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4866","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he mentioned the entire hadith, and up to this point he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah! Advise me. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you to adopt the fear of Allah, for it is the most beautifying for all your affairs."" I said: Tell me more! He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an and remember Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for it will be a mention for you in the heavens and a light for you on the earth."" I said: Advise me more. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Always remain silent, for it drives away Satan and helps you in matters of your religion."" I said: Tell me more. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid excessive laughter, for it kills the heart and removes the light from the face."" I said: Advise me more. The narrator says, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Speak the truth, even if it is bitter."" I said: Tell me more. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fear the blame of any blamer in the matter of Allah."" I said: Tell me more. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The knowledge of your own faults should prevent you from finding fault with others."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4867","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Dharr! Shall I not tell you of two qualities which are very light on the back (in terms of a person's actions) but very heavy on the scale?"" He narrates, I said, Yes! Tell me. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remaining silent and adopting good character. By the One in whose hand is my soul! The creation has not performed two deeds like these."" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4868","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was cursing one of his slaves. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at him and said: ""(Can) one who curses and the truthful (Siddiqeen) be together? By the Lord of the Ka'bah! Never."" So Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) freed some of his slaves that day (as expiation), then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: I will not do so again. Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all five hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Hasan, narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4869","(Aslam, the freed slave of Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that one day Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, went to Abu Bakr Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, and found him pulling his tongue. (Seeing this scene) Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: May Allah forgive you! Leave it. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, replied: It has brought me to the pits of destruction. Its chain is authentic, narrated by Malik."
"4870","It is narrated from ‘Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Guarantee me six things from yourselves and I will guarantee you Paradise: When you speak, speak the truth; when you make a promise, fulfill it; when something is entrusted to you, return it; guard your private parts; lower your gaze; and restrain your hands (from injustice).” Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"4871","It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Ghanm and Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best servants of Allah are those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered. And the worst among Allah's servants are the tale-bearers, those who create discord between loved ones, and those who accuse the innocent of evil."" Hasan, narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4872","On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanum and Asma bint Yazid, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: “The best servants of Allah are those who remember Allah when they are seen, while the worst of Allah’s servants are gossipers, those who separate between loved ones, and those who accuse those indifferent (of sins) of evil.” Hasan, narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shub al-Iman."
"4873","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that two men performed the Zuhr or Asr prayer while they were fasting. When the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, had finished the prayer, he said: ""Both of you should repeat your ablution, repeat the prayer, complete your fast, and make up for it on another day."" Both of them asked: O Messenger of Allah! Why? He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""You have backbitten such-and-such person."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4874","Abu Sa'id and Jabir (may Allah be pleased with them) report that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Backbiting is more severe than adultery."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! How is backbiting more severe than adultery?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man commits adultery, then he repents, and Allah accepts his repentance."" In another narration: ""He repents, and Allah forgives him. Whereas the one who commits backbiting is not forgiven until the person about whom he backbit has forgiven him."" Its chain is very weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman, also."
"4875","Abu Saeed and Jabir narrate that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Backbiting is more serious than adultery?"" The Companions said: Messenger of Allah! How is backbiting more serious than adultery? The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Indeed, if a person commits adultery, he repents and Allah accepts his repentance."" While the one who backbites is not forgiven even if the person who has been backbited forgives him."
"4876","And in the narration of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), it is stated: ""The one who commits adultery repents, whereas there is no repentance for the one who backbites."" (Because he does not consider it important that this is also a sin, and thus he is unable to repent.) Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all three hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4877","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The expiation for backbiting is that you pray for forgiveness for the one you have backbitten; say: O Allah! Forgive us and him."" (Bayhaqi in Al-Da'awat Al-Kabir). And he said: There is weakness in its chain of narration. Its chain is weak. It is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Al-Da'awat Al-Kabir."
"4878","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away and wealth came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) from Alaa bin Hadrami (may Allah be pleased with him), Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Whoever had a debt upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) or to whom he had promised to give something, let him come to us (we will pay that debt and fulfill his promise)."" Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I said, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) promised me that he would give me such and such and such,"" and Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) spread his hands three times. Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said that he gave me a handful, and when I counted them, they were five hundred. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Take the same amount two more times."" Agreed upon."
"4879","Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I saw the Messenger of Allah with a (reddish) white complexion, and some of his hair had turned white, and Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) resembled him (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him). He (the Prophet) ordered thirteen she-camels for us. When we went to take them, the news of his death reached us, so we did not get anything. However, when Abu Bakr assumed the responsibility of the caliphate, he said: If anyone has any promise from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), let him come. I went to him and informed him, so he ordered that camels be given to us. Sahih, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4880","Abdullah bin Abi Hamsa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Before the declaration of Prophethood, I bought something from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and there was some payment left that I owed him. I promised to bring the remaining amount to him at that same place, but I forgot. After three days, I remembered (and went), and he was still at that place. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You put me through hardship; I have been waiting for you here for three days."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4881","Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man makes a promise to his brother with the intention of fulfilling it, but he is unable to fulfill the promise and does not reach at the appointed time, then there is no sin upon him."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4882","Abdullah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One day my mother called me while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was present in our house. My mother said: Listen, come here, I will give you something. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: ""What do you intend to give him?"" She replied: I intend to give him a date. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! If you had not given him anything, a lie would have been recorded against you."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4883","It is narrated from Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If a person makes an appointment with another man, but one of them does not arrive by the time of prayer, and the one who has come goes to perform the prayer, then there is no sin upon him."" Weak, narrated by Razeen."
"4884","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not act formally with us (he lived among us informally), to the extent that he would say to my younger brother: ""Abu Umair! What did the little bird do?"" Abu Umair had a small bird with which he used to play, and it died. Agreed upon."
"4885","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! You joke with us?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""I only speak the truth."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4886","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for a mount, so he said: ""I will mount you on the offspring of a she-camel."" The man said: ""What will I do with the offspring of a she-camel?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""She-camels only give birth to camels."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4887","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""O two-eared one!"" Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood and Tirmidhi."
"4888","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to an old woman: ""No old woman will enter Paradise."" She asked: What is the reason for them (being prevented)? And she used to recite the Qur'an. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Do you not recite the Qur'an? Indeed, We have created them (the maidens of Paradise) in a special manner, then made them virgins."" Razin. In Sharh al-Sunnah, the wording is from Mishkat. Weak, narrated by Razin and in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4889","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a Bedouin named Zahir bin Haram used to bring gifts from the desert for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he intended to return, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give him (provisions). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Zahir is our agent in the desert and we are his caretakers in the city."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love him, even though he was not handsome. One day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while he was selling his goods, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced him from behind, and he could not see who it was. He said: ""Let me go, who is this?"" He looked from one side and recognized that it was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he recognized him, he pressed his back firmly against the blessed chest of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to say: ""Who will buy this slave?"" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, you will find me of little value."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""But you are not of little value in the sight of Allah."" Its chain is authentic. It is narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4890","Awf bin Malik Ashja'i (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I presented myself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk. He was in a small leather tent. I greeted him with salam, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to my salam and said: ""Come inside."" I said: O Messenger of Allah! Should I come in completely (all of me)? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Come in completely (all of you)."" I went inside. ‘Uthman bin Abi ‘Atikah (the narrator) says: He said, ""Should I come in completely into the small tent?"" Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4891","Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he heard the voice of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) raised. When he entered, he caught hold of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) in order to slap her, and he said: I do not see you raising your voice over the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began to prevent Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and he left in a state of anger. When Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) had gone out, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Did you see how I protected you from that man (i.e., Abu Bakr)?” The narrator says: After a few days, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came again and sought permission to enter, and he found them (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) in a state of reconciliation, and he said to them: Include me in your reconciliation just as you included me in your quarrel. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “We have done so, we have done so.” Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4892","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not quarrel with your (Muslim) brother, nor joke with him in a hurtful manner, nor make a promise to him which you will break."" __REF_N__ Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4893","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it was asked from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Who is the most honorable person among the people? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most honorable among them in the sight of Allah is the one who is most pious and God-fearing among them."" The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: We are not asking you about this. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then the most honorable person is Yusuf (peace be upon him), the Prophet of Allah, son of the Prophet of Allah, grandson of the Prophet of Allah, great-grandson of the Friend of Allah (Ibrahim, peace be upon him)."" The companions said: We are not asking you about this. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Are you asking me about the Arab tribes?"" They said: Yes! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those among you who were best in the days of ignorance are the best among you in Islam, provided they gain understanding (of the etiquette of Shariah)."" Agreed upon."
"4894","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble is Yusuf, son of Yaqub, son of Ishaq, son of Ibrahim (peace be upon them)."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4895","Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the day of the Battle of Hunayn, Abu Sufyan bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) was holding the reins of your (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) mule. When the polytheists surrounded you from all sides, you dismounted and said: ""I am the Prophet, there is no lie in this, and I am the son of Abdul Muttalib."" The narrator states: On that day, no one was seen braver than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) among all the people. Agreed upon."
"4896","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked him: ""Who is the best person among the creation?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""He is Ibrahim (Abraham) (peace be upon him)."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4897","Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not exaggerate in praising me as the Christians exaggerated in praising the son of Mary. I am only His servant, so say: the servant of Allah and His Messenger."" Agreed upon."
"4898","It is narrated from Iyad bin Himar Mujashi’i (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah has revealed to me that you should adopt humility so that no one boasts over another and no one oppresses another.” Narrated by Muslim."
"4899","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""People should stop boasting about their deceased ancestors; they are merely coals of Hell, or they are more insignificant in the sight of Allah than a dung beetle that pushes filth with its nose. Indeed, Allah has removed the pride and arrogance of the Age of Ignorance regarding ancestors from you. Now, (the one who is honored) is either a pious, righteous believer or a wretched sinner. All people are the children of Adam, and Adam was (created) from dust."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4900","It is narrated from Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Shukhair (may Allah have mercy on him), who (narrates from his father): I was present with the delegation of Banu Amir in the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). We said: ""You are our master."" He replied: ""The Master is Allah."" Then we said: ""You are superior to us in virtue and greater than us."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say what you are saying, or say part of your words, and let not Satan embolden you (to make up things)."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood."
"4901","Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In this world, honor is through wealth, while with Allah (in the Hereafter), honor is through piety."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."
"4902","Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever ascribes himself to the lineage of the days of ignorance (and boasts about it), tell him to bite his father's private part and do not say this as a euphemism."" Chain is weak. Narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah, Ahmad, and al-Bukhari in al-Adab al-Mufrad."
"4903","Abdur Rahman bin Abi Aqbah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Abu Aqbah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he was a freed slave of the people of Persia. He said: I participated in the Battle of Uhud with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I struck a polytheist and said: Receive (endure) this from me, I am of Persian descent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards me and said: ""Why did you not say, 'Receive (endure) this from me, and I am an Ansari, a young man.'"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4904","Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Whoever supports and assists his people unjustly is like a camel that falls into a well and is pulled out by its tail."" Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4905","Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I asked, “O Messenger of Allah! What is ‘asabiyyah (tribalism)?” He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “That you help your people in wrongdoing.” (Weak chain), narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4906","Suraqah bin Malik bin Ju'sham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said while addressing us in a sermon: ""The best defender among you is the one who defends his family, provided he does not commit a sin."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4907","It is narrated from Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He is not one of us who calls towards tribalism, he is not one of us who fights for tribalism, and he is not one of us who dies upon tribalism."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4908","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Love for something makes one blind and deaf."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4909","‘Ubadah bin Katheer al-Shami narrates from his (Palestinian) wife named Faseelah, who said: I heard my father narrating, I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about an issue, saying: O Messenger of Allah! Is it also considered partisanship (‘asabiyyah) that a man loves his own people? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “No, rather partisanship is that a man supports and helps his people in wrongdoing.” Weak, narrated by Ahmad and Ibn Majah."
"4910","Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These genealogies (lineage, tribe) of yours are not a cause of disgrace for anyone. You are all the children of Adam and you are all equal to each other just as one sa’ (measure) is equal to another sa’. No one has superiority over another except in religion and piety. It is enough of a disgrace for a person that he is foul-mouthed, obscene in speech, and miserly."" Hasan, narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"4911","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who is most deserving of my good conduct?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""Your mother."" He asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Your mother."" He asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Your mother."" He asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Your father."" In another narration, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Your mother, then your mother, then your mother, then your father, then the closest of your relatives, then the next closest."" Agreed upon."
"4912","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May his nose be rubbed in dust, may his nose be rubbed in dust, may his nose be rubbed in dust!"" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Whose? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who finds one or both of his parents in old age and then does not enter Paradise (by treating them well)."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4913","Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: My mother came to me while she was a polytheist. This was at the time when the treaty (of Hudaybiyyah) was made with the Quraysh. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Indeed, my mother has come to me and she desires good treatment from me, so should I maintain ties of kinship with her? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes! Maintain ties of kinship with her."" Agreed upon."
"4914","Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The family of Abu so-and-so are not my friends and supporters; my supporter is Allah and the righteous believers. However, there is a kinship with them which I will maintain through ties of kinship."" Agreed upon."
"4915","Mughira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah has made disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, miserliness, and asking (begging) forbidden for you, and He has disliked for you idle talk, excessive questioning (about people's affairs), and wasting wealth."" Agreed upon."
"4916","Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's reviling his parents is a major sin."" The Companions asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Does a man revile his own parents?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Yes, he abuses another man's father, so (in return) that man abuses his father, and he abuses another man's mother, so (in return) that man abuses his mother."" Agreed upon."
"4917","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, after a man's father passes away, maintaining ties with his father's friends is the greatest act of goodness."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4918","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes that his provision be expanded and his life be prolonged, let him maintain the ties of kinship."" Agreed upon."
"4919","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah created the creation, and when He finished with it, the womb (rahm) stood up and held onto the back of the Most Merciful (Ar-Rahman). He (the Most Merciful) said: 'What is this?' It (the womb) said: 'This is the place of one who seeks refuge with You from severing ties.' He said: 'Are you not pleased that I will maintain ties with the one who maintains ties with you, and I will sever ties with the one who severs ties with you?' The womb said: 'Yes, my Lord, I am pleased.' He said: 'Then that is for you.' "" Agreed upon."
"4920","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The womb (rahm) is derived from the Most Merciful (Rahman). Allah said: 'Whoever maintains ties with you, I will maintain ties with him, and whoever severs ties with you, I will sever ties with him.'"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4921","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The womb is suspended from the Throne. It says: Whoever maintains me, Allah will maintain him, and whoever severs me, Allah will sever him."" Agreed upon."
"4922","Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The one who severs the ties of kinship will not enter Paradise."" Agreed upon."
"4923","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The one who reciprocates kindness only in response to kindness is not truly upholding the ties of kinship; rather, the one who truly upholds the ties of kinship is the one who, when his ties are severed, still maintains them."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4924","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah! I have some relatives with whom I maintain ties of kinship, but they sever relations with me; I treat them well, but they treat me badly; I am patient with them, but they wrong me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If what you say is true, then it is as if you are putting hot ashes in their mouths. As long as you continue in this way, you will have Allah’s support against them."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4925","Thauban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplication changes destiny, good conduct increases lifespan, and indeed a person is deprived of sustenance because of committing sins."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"4926","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and I heard a recitation there, so I asked: Who is this (reciting)? They said: It is Haritha bin Nu’man. This is the reward for good conduct, the reward for good conduct is like this."" And he was the one who treated his mother with the best conduct. Al-Bayhaqi narrated it in Shu’ab al-Iman, and in another narration, instead of ""I entered Paradise,"" the words are: ""I saw myself in Paradise in a dream."" Its chain is weak. It is narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah and by al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"4927","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The pleasure of the father is the pleasure of the Lord, and the displeasure of the father is the displeasure of the Lord."" Its chain is good; narrated by Tirmidhi."
"4928","It is narrated from Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to him and said: I have a wife, but my mother is ordering me to divorce her. (Hearing this) Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The father is the best door of Paradise; if you wish, safeguard this door, and if you wish, waste it."" Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."
"4929","Bahz bin Hakim narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, who said: I asked, O Messenger of Allah! With whom should I behave kindly? He ﷺ said: ""With your mother."" I asked, then who? He ﷺ said: ""With your mother."" I asked, then who? He ﷺ said: ""With your mother."" I asked, then who? He ﷺ said: ""With your mother."" I asked, then with whom? He ﷺ said: ""With your father, then the nearest and then the next nearest relatives (behave kindly with them)."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4930","Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, says: I am Allah and I am the Most Merciful (Rahman). I created the womb (rahm) and derived its name from My Name (Rahman). Whoever maintains its ties, I will maintain ties with him, and whoever severs it, shall I deprive him (of My mercy)?"" Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4931","Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Mercy is not sent down upon a people among whom there is a person who severs the ties of kinship."" Its chain of narration is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4932","Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Oppression, rebellion, and severing ties of kinship are such sins that Allah punishes their perpetrator in this world, and in addition, reserves punishment for him in the Hereafter as well."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4933","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The one who reminds others of his favors, the one who is disobedient to his parents, and the habitual wine drinker will not enter Paradise."" Its chain is good. Narrated by al-Nasa'i and al-Darimi."
"4934","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Learn your lineage to the extent that you maintain the ties of kinship, for maintaining the ties of kinship brings love among relatives, increases wealth, and prolongs life."" (Tirmidhi), and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4935","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have committed a very great sin, so is there any room for repentance for me? The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do you have a mother?"" He replied, No. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do you have a maternal aunt?"" He replied, Yes. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Treat her kindly."" Its chain is authentic; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4936","Abu Usaid Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: While we were in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), a man from the tribe of Banu Salamah came and said: O Messenger of Allah! Is there any way of showing kindness to my parents after their death through which I can continue to be good to them? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes! Pray for them, seek forgiveness for them, fulfill their pledges after them, maintain the ties of kinship which were dependent on them, and honor their friends."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Ibn Majah."
"4937","Abu Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the place of Ji‘ranah distributing meat. Suddenly, a woman came until she reached close to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he spread his cloak for her, and she sat on it. I asked, ""Who is she?"" They replied: ""She is the Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) foster mother."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4938","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Three men were traveling during a certain period, rain came, and they took shelter in a cave in a mountain. Meanwhile, a rock fell from the mountain and closed the mouth of their cave. So they said to each other: Review your deeds which you have done purely for the sake of Allah, then supplicate to Allah through them, perhaps He will remove this distress (the rock). One of them said: O Allah! I had elderly parents and small children, and I was responsible for their sustenance. When I would return in the evening with the livestock, I would milk the animals and present the milk to my parents before my children. Once, I went far into the forest, so I returned home late in the evening and found both of them asleep. As usual, I milked the animals, then brought the vessel of milk and stood by their heads. I did not consider it appropriate to wake them, nor did I want to give it to my children before them, while the children were crying with hunger at my feet. This situation remained until morning. (O Allah!) If You know that I did this for Your pleasure, then make a way for us so that we may see the sky. Allah opened a way for them until they could see the sky.The second said: O Allah! I had a cousin whom I loved as much as any man can love a woman. I expressed my desire to commit an evil act with her, but she refused, until I gave her one hundred dinars. I worked hard and collected one hundred dinars and brought them to her, and when I sat between her legs (to commit the evil act), she said: O servant of Allah! Fear Allah and do not break the seal unlawfully. (Upon hearing this) I stood up from her. O Allah! If You know that I did this for Your pleasure, then open a way for us! Allah opened some of the way for them.The third person said: O Allah! I had hired a laborer for a measure (six ratls) of rice as his wage. When he completed his work, he said: Pay me my due. When I offered him his due, he considered it insignificant and left it and went away. I invested it in agriculture until I gathered cows and a herdsman from it. He came to me and said: Fear Allah and do not wrong me, and give me my right. I said: Take these cows and the herdsman. He said: Fear Allah! Do not mock me. I said: I am not mocking you, take these cows and the herdsman. So he took them and went away. If You know that I did this to seek Your pleasure, then open the remaining way for us. So Allah opened the way for them (and removed their distress)."" __QUR_N__ Agreed upon."
"4939","It is narrated from Muawiyah bin Jahimah that Jahimah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I want to consult you about participating in jihad."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Do you have a mother?"" He replied, ""Yes!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Go! Stay with her, for Paradise is at her feet."" Its chain is authentic; narrated by Ahmad, al-Nasa'i, and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4940","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I had a wife whom I liked, but Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) disliked her. He said to me: ""Divorce her."" I refused, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned this incident to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Divorce her."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"4941","It is narrated from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked: O Messenger of Allah! What right do parents have over their children? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Both of them are your Paradise (cause) and your Hell (cause)."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"4942","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant’s parents, or one of them, passes away while he was disobedient to them, and then (after their death) he continues to pray for them and seeks forgiveness for them, so Allah records him as one who does good to his parents."" Weak, narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4943","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever spends the morning obeying Allah regarding his parents' rights, the doors of Paradise are opened for him, and if there is only one (parent), then (only) one door. And whoever spends the morning disobeying Allah regarding his parents' rights, the doors of Hell are opened for him, and if there is only one (parent), then (only) one door."" A man asked, ""Even if they wrong him?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Even if they wrong him, even if they wrong him, and even if they wrong him."" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4944","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When a righteous child looks at his parents with a gaze of mercy, Allah writes for him, in exchange for every such look, the reward of an accepted Hajj."" The companions, may Allah be pleased with them, asked: ""Even if he looks a hundred times every day?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: ""Yes, Allah is greater (than what can be imagined) and purer (from every imperfection)."" Its chain is fabricated. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4945","Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Apart from disobedience to parents, Allah forgives as many sins as He wills, because He punishes the one who commits this (sin) in this very life before death."" Its chain is weak; it was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4946","Saeed bin Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The right of the elder brother over his younger brothers is like the right of the father over his children."" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all five hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4947","Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not show mercy to the one who does not show mercy to people."" Agreed upon."
"4948","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked, ""Do you kiss children? For we do not kiss them."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""I have no control over you if Allah has removed mercy from your heart (that I could bring it back)."" Agreed upon."
"4949","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: A woman came to me and she had two daughters with her. She asked me (for something), and I had only one date, so I gave it to her. She divided it between her two daughters and did not eat anything herself. Then she stood up and left. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, so I mentioned this to him. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is tested with these daughters in any way and treats them well, they will be a shield for him from Hellfire."" Agreed upon."
"4950","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever brought up two daughters until they reached maturity, he will come on the Day of Resurrection like this with me,"" and he joined his fingers together. Narrated by Muslim."
"4951","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who looks after the needs of a widow and a poor person is like the one who fights in the way of Allah."" And I think that he (peace and blessings be upon him) also said: ""He is like the one who stands (in prayer at night) without tiring, and like the one who fasts continuously without breaking his fast."" Agreed upon."
"4952","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I and the one who takes care of an orphan, whether the orphan is his own or someone else’s, will be in Paradise like this.” And he (peace and blessings be upon him) gestured with his index and middle fingers and then made a slight gap between them. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"4953","Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “You will find the believers, in their mutual mercy, love, and kindness towards one another, like a single body; when one limb suffers, the whole body responds with wakefulness and fever.” Agreed upon."
"4954","Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “All believers are like a single body; if its eye is in pain, the whole body feels pain, and if its head is afflicted, the whole body feels the affliction.” Narrated by Muslim."
"4955","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A believer to another believer is like a building, each part of which strengthens the other."" Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced the fingers of one hand with those of the other. Agreed upon."
"4956","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when a beggar or a needy person would come to him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: ""Intercede (on behalf of others), you will be rewarded, and Allah will decree what He wills through the tongue of His Messenger."" Agreed upon."
"4957","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Help your (Muslim) brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed."" A man asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! I will help the oppressed, but how can I help the oppressor?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""By preventing him from oppression, that is your helping him."" Agreed upon."
"4958","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he neither oppresses him nor hands him over (to the oppressor). Whoever is engaged in fulfilling the need of his brother, Allah will fulfill his need, and whoever removes a difficulty from a Muslim, Allah will remove one of the difficulties of the Day of Resurrection from him. And whoever conceals (the faults of) a Muslim, Allah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection."" Agreed upon."
"4959","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not oppress him, nor does he abandon him helpless, nor does he despise him. Taqwa is here,"" and he pointed to his chest three times. ""It is enough evil for a man that he despises his Muslim brother. The blood, wealth, and honor of every Muslim are forbidden to another Muslim."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4960","Iyad bin Hamar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise are of three types: a just, charitable, and successful ruler; (second) a person who is kind and gentle-hearted towards every relative (especially) and every Muslim (generally); and (third) a family man who refrains from forbidden things and from begging. As for the people of Hell, they are of five types: the weak one who has no sense (by which he can avoid evil), those who are under your authority, who have no desire for (lawful) family and wealth, the treacherous person who, if he covets even a small thing, betrays it, the man who deceives you morning and evening (at every opportunity) regarding your family and your wealth."" And he mentioned the miser or the liar. ""And the ill-mannered person who is foul-mouthed."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4961","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! None of you can be a believer until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."" Agreed upon."
"4962","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Allah! He is not a believer, by Allah! He is not a believer, by Allah! He is not a believer."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who (is not a believer)? He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The one whose neighbor is not safe from his mischief."" Agreed upon."
"4963","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person whose neighbor is not safe from his mischief will not enter Paradise."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4964","Aisha and Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Gabriel continued to advise me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."" Agreed upon."
"4965","Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are three, then two of you should not converse secretly excluding the third until you join other people, for this manner will grieve him (the third person)."" Agreed upon."
"4966","It is narrated from Tamim Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said three times: ""Religion is sincerity and goodwill."" We asked, ""For whom?"" He said: ""For Allah, for His Book, for His Messenger, for the leaders of the Muslims, and for the common Muslims."" Narrated by Muslim."
"4967","Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on establishing prayer, giving zakat, and being sincere to every Muslim. Agreed upon."
"4968","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard Abul Qasim, the truthful and trustworthy (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: ""Mercy is taken away only from a wretched person."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"4969","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Most Merciful shows mercy to those who are merciful. Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One in the heavens will show mercy to you."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Tirmidhi."
"4970","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy to our young ones, does not respect our elders, does not enjoin good, and does not forbid evil, is not from among us."" (Tirmidhi), and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4971","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever honors an elderly person because of his old age, Allah will appoint someone to honor him in his old age."" Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4972","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Honoring an elderly Muslim, honoring such a memorizer of the Qur'an who does not act with excess, and honoring a just ruler are from the reverence of Allah."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4973","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the houses among the Muslims is the house in which there is an orphan and he is treated well, and the worst of the houses among the Muslims is the house in which there is an orphan and he is treated badly."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"4974","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever, for the sake of Allah’s pleasure, passes his hand over the head of an orphan, then for every hair that his hand passes over, he will receive a good deed. And whoever treats well any orphan boy or girl under his care, he and I will be like this in Paradise."" And he joined his two fingers together. (Narrated by Ahmad, Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Also narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi.)"
"4975","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever includes an orphan in his food and drink (on his dining spread), Allah makes Paradise obligatory for him, provided he has not committed an unforgivable sin. And whoever takes care of three daughters or as many sisters, gives them good upbringing, shows mercy to them until he fulfills all their needs, Allah makes Paradise obligatory for that person."" A man asked: O Messenger of Allah! What about the one who takes care of two? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes, even two."" Even if he had asked, what about one? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would have said: Even one. ""And if Allah takes away two precious things from a person, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by two precious things? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""His two eyes."" Its chain is weak, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4976","Jabir bin Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A man's good upbringing of his child is better for him than giving a sa’ in charity."" Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is gharib, and Nasih the narrator is not strong according to the scholars of hadith. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"4977","Ayub bin Musa narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The best gift parents give to their children is their good upbringing."" Tirmidhi, Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman. And Imam Tirmidhi said: In my view, this hadith is mursal. Its chain is weak, narrated by Tirmidhi and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4978","Auf bin Malik Ashja'i (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I and the woman with a darkened face (the widow whose face has become dark due to hard work) will be like this on the Day of Resurrection."" And Yazid bin Zurai' pointed towards his middle finger and index finger. ""Also, a woman of status and beauty whose husband passes away and she does not marry because of her orphaned children until they grow up or die."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4979","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a daughter and does not bury her alive, nor humiliates her, nor prefers his son over her, Allah will admit him to Paradise."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4980","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""If someone backbites his Muslim brother in his presence and he is able to support and defend him, and he does so, then Allah will support and defend him in this world and the Hereafter. But if he does not support him despite being able to do so, then Allah will leave him without help in this world and the Hereafter."" Weak, even fabricated. Narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4981","Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not allow his (Muslim) brother to be backbitten in his absence, it is a right upon Allah to free him from the fire of Hell."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4982","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever defends the honor of his Muslim brother, it is incumbent upon Allah to defend him from Hell on the Day of Resurrection."" Then he recited this verse: ""Helping the believers is incumbent upon Us."" Its chain is weak, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"4983","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever abandons a Muslim in a place where his honor and dignity are being violated, Allah will abandon him in a place where he will be in need of help. And whoever helps a Muslim in a place where his honor and dignity are being violated, Allah will help him in a place where he would like to be helped."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4984","Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees a fault (of someone) and conceals it, he is like the one who brings a buried-alive person back to life."" Ahmad, Tirmidhi, and they declared it authentic. Hasan, narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"4985","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, each one of you is a mirror to his (Muslim) brother; if he sees any fault in him, he should remove it from him."" __REF_N__ Tirmidhi, and he has declared it weak. In the narration of Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood: ""A believer is a mirror to another believer, and a believer is the brother of another believer; he does not let him suffer loss and he protects him (his life, wealth, and honor) in his absence."" __REF_N__ Weak Jaza, narrated by Tirmidhi. Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4986","Mu’adh bin Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever protects the honor of a believer from a hypocrite, Allah will send an angel who will protect his flesh from the fire of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever accuses a Muslim of something in order to disgrace him, Allah will detain him on the Bridge of Hell until he is cleared of what he said.” Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4987","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The best companion in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best neighbor in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."" Tirmidhi, Darimi, and Tirmidhi said: This hadith is hasan ghareeb. Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Darimi."
"4988","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah! How will I know whether I am good or bad? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you hear your neighbors saying that you are good, then you are good, and when you hear them saying that you are bad, then you are bad."" Its chain is authentic, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"4989","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Treat people according to their status and rank."" Its chain of narration is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"4990","It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Abi Qurad (may Allah be pleased with him) that one day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, and his companions (may Allah be pleased with them) began to rub the water from his ablution on their bodies. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: ""What made you do this?"" They replied: The love of Allah and His Messenger. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to love Allah and His Messenger, or that Allah and His Messenger love him, then when he speaks, he should speak the truth; when something is entrusted to him, he should return it; and he should treat his neighbors and those he associates with kindly."" Its chain is weak. It is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4991","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""He is not a believer who eats his fill while his close neighbor is hungry."" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated both hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4992","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Such-and-such woman is well-known for the abundance of her prayers, fasts, and charity, but she harms her neighbors with her sharp tongue."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""She is in Hell."" The man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Such-and-such woman is well-known for the scarcity of her prayers, fasts, and charity, and she gives only a few pieces of cheese in charity, but she does not harm her neighbors with her tongue."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""She is in Paradise."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4993","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood by some people who were sitting, and said: ""Shall I not inform you about your worst and best people?"" The narrator states, they remained silent. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this three times, so a man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Certainly, do inform us about the best among our worst."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one from whom good is expected and people are safe from his evil, while the worst among you is the one from whom no good is expected and people are not safe from his evil."" (Tirmidhi, Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman) And Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is Hasan Sahih. Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4994","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah has distributed your character among you just as He has distributed your wealth among you. Indeed, Allah gives the world to every person, whether He likes him or dislikes him, but He gives religion only to the one whom He loves. Whoever Allah grants religion to, then (understand that) he is a beloved person of Allah. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! No servant can be a Muslim until his heart and his tongue become Muslim, and he does not become a believer until his neighbor is safe from his mischief."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4995","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is a place of affection (entirely affectionate), and there is no good in the one who does not show affection to others nor do others show affection to him."" Ahmad, and Imam Bayhaqi have both narrated these hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Sahih, narrated by Ahmad and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4996","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fulfills the need of any of my followers through which he wishes to make him happy, then he has made me happy; whoever makes me happy has made Allah happy; and whoever makes Allah happy, Allah will admit him into Paradise."" Its chain is fabricated. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4997","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever helps a person in distress, Allah writes for him seventy-three (73) forgivenesses; one of them is for the rectification of all his affairs, while the remaining seventy-two (72) will be a means of raising his ranks on the Day of Resurrection."" Its chain is fabricated. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4998","Anas and Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Creation is Allah’s dependents, and the most beloved of creation to Allah is the one who treats His dependents well."" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all three hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"4999","Narrated by Anas and Abdullah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The creatures are the children of Allah (under his guardianship), and among the creatures, the one who treats his children well is the one whom Allah likes the most.” The authority of Zaeef Jaza, the narration of al-Bayhaqi in Shab al-Iman."
"5000","Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the case between two neighbors will be presented first."" Hasan, narrated by Ahmad."
"5001","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man complained to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, about the hardness of his heart. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Stroke the head of the orphan and feed the poor."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Ahmad."
"5002","It is narrated from Suraqah bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the best charity?"" It is to give charity to your daughter who returns to you (due to divorce or similar reasons) and has no one else to earn for her except you."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"5003","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Souls are like recruited troops; those who became familiar with one another (in the world of souls) will be friendly with each other (in this world), and those who felt alienation will remain in disagreement."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5004","And Imam Muslim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated it from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him). Narrated by Muslim."
"5005","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibreel and says: 'Indeed, I love so-and-so, so you also love him.' He said: Jibreel loves him, then he announces among the inhabitants of the heavens: 'Indeed, Allah loves so-and-so, so you also love him.' The inhabitants of the heavens love him, then acceptance is placed for him among the people of the earth. And when Allah dislikes a servant, He calls Jibreel and says: 'Indeed, I dislike so-and-so, so you also dislike him.' Jibreel dislikes him, then he announces among the inhabitants of the heavens that Allah dislikes so-and-so, so you also dislike him. He said: They dislike him, then hatred for him is placed in the hearts of the people of the earth."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5006","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah will say on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who loved one another for My greatness and glory? Today I will shelter them in My shade, on a day when there is no shade except My shade."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5007","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man set out to visit a (Muslim) brother of his in another town. So Allah appointed an angel on his way who waited for him. (When he passed by the angel,) the angel said: Where are you intending to go? The man replied: I am going to visit a (Muslim) brother of mine in that town. The angel asked: Is there any favor he has done to you which you are going to repay? He said: There is no other reason except that I love him for the sake of Allah. The (angel) said: I am a messenger to you from Allah to inform you that just as you love him for the sake of Allah, so Allah loves you. ""Narrated by Muslim."""
"5008","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about a person who loves some people but has not joined them (in companionship or in knowledge and deeds)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A person will be with those whom he loves."" Agreed upon."
"5009","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) come?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Woe to you! What have you prepared for it?"" He replied, ""My preparation is only that I love Allah and His Messenger."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You will be with those whom you love."" Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I have not seen the Muslims rejoice at anything more than they did at this statement after accepting Islam."" Agreed upon."
"5010","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a good companion and a bad companion is like that of a musk seller and a blacksmith who blows the bellows. The musk seller may either give you some (musk) as a gift, or you may buy it from him, or at least you will get a pleasant fragrance from him. As for the one who blows the bellows, he may burn your clothes, or you will get a foul smell from him."" Agreed upon."
"5011","Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Allah the Exalted says: For those who love each other for My sake, meet each other for My sake, and spend on each other for My sake, My love becomes obligatory.” (Malik) And in the narration of Tirmidhi, it is stated: “Allah the Exalted says: For those who love each other for the sake of My majesty and greatness, there are pulpits of light, which even the Prophets and martyrs will envy.” Sahih, narrated by Malik and al-Tirmidhi."
"5012","Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the servants of Allah are some people who are neither prophets nor martyrs, but on the Day of Resurrection, even the prophets and martyrs will envy their rank and status with Allah."" The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: O Messenger of Allah! Please tell us who these people are. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are those who love one another not because of any family relationship nor because of any financial dealings, but they love and interact with each other solely for the sake of Allah and in obedience to the Qur'an. By Allah! Their faces will be radiant and they will be upon pulpits of light. When others will be afraid, they will not fear, and when others will be grieved, they will not grieve."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""Behold! Indeed, there will be no fear upon the friends of Allah, nor will they grieve."" Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5013","And he (Imam Baghawi) narrated it in Sharh al-Sunnah with the wording of Misbahih through the chain of Abu Malik with some additions, and likewise it is also in Shu'ab al-Iman. Hasan, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah, Misbahih al-Sunnah, and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5014","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Abu Dharr! Which part (aspect) of faith is the strongest and most firm?"" He replied, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Loving and supporting each other for the sake of Allah, loving for the sake of Allah, and harboring aversion for the sake of Allah."" Weak, narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5015","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim visits his (Muslim) brother who is ill or meets him, Allah Almighty says: Your life in the Hereafter has become good, your walking has become good, and you have made a place for yourself in Paradise."" (Tirmidhi), and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5016","Miqdam bin Ma’dikarib, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""When a man loves his (Muslim) brother, he should inform him that he loves him."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Tirmidhi."
"5017","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while some people were with him. One of those people said: I love this person for the sake of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have you informed him?"" He replied: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go to him and tell him."" So he went to that person and told him (that I love you for the sake of Allah). He replied: May the One for whose sake you love me, love you in return. The narrator states: Then that man returned, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked him, so he informed him of the reply. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will be with the one whom you love, and you will receive the reward you desired."" (Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman). And in the narration of Tirmidhi: ""A person will be with whom he loves, and he will receive the recompense for what he has done."" Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman and al-Tirmidhi."
"5018","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""You should only keep the company of a believer, and only a pious person should eat your food."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi, Abu Dawood, and al-Darimi."
"5019","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man is upon the religion of his friend, so each of you should look at whom he befriends."" Ahmad, Tirmidhi, Abu Dawood, Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman. And Imam Tirmidhi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This hadith is hasan ghareeb, and Imam Nawawi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Its chain of narration is authentic. Hasan, narrated by Ahmad, Tirmidhi, Abu Dawood, and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5020","Yazid bin Ni‘amah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a man establishes brotherhood with another man, he should ask him about his name, his father's name, and his tribe, because this increases love (friendship)."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5021","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us and said: ""Do you know which deeds are most beloved to Allah?"" One of the companions said: Prayer, zakat, and another said: Jihad. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved deed to Allah is to love for the sake of Allah and to hate for the sake of Allah."" (Ahmad) And Abu Dawood narrated the last part. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood."
"5022","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves someone for the sake of Allah, then he has honored his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad."
"5023","It is narrated from Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Shall I not tell you about the best among you?"" The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Please do tell us."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you are those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered."" Hasan, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"5024","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If two servants love each other for the sake of Allah Almighty, one is in the east and the other in the west, then on the Day of Resurrection Allah will gather them both together and will say: This is the one whom you used to love for My pleasure."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5025","Abu Razin (Luqait bin Amir bin Sabrah, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: ""Shall I not tell you about the foundation of this religion through which you will attain goodness in both religion and the world? Join the gatherings of the people of remembrance, and when you are alone, then keep your tongue busy with the remembrance of Allah as much as you can, and love for the sake of Allah and hate for the sake of Allah. Abu Razin! Do you know? When a man sets out to visit his (Muslim) brother, seventy thousand angels walk with him and all of them pray for him and say: Our Lord! He has established a relationship for Your pleasure, so join him (with Your mercy and forgiveness). If you can engage your body in these deeds, then do so."" Its chain is weak; it is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5026","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: ""In Paradise there are pillars of ruby, upon them are chambers of emerald, their doors are open, and they shine like bright stars."" The noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who will reside in them? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who love each other for the sake of Allah, who sit together for the sake of Allah, and who meet each other for the sake of Allah."" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all three hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5027","Abu Ayyub Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is not permissible for a man to sever relations with his (Muslim) brother for more than three days; when they meet, each turns away from the other, and the better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace (salam)."" Agreed upon."
"5028","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the greatest falsehood. Do not search for each other's faults, nor spy on one another. Do not bid against each other to raise prices, nor envy one another, nor bear malice, nor sever relations. And O servants of Allah! Be brothers to one another."" In another narration it is stated: ""(And do not try to outdo one another out of envy)."" Agreed upon."
"5029","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The gates of Paradise are opened on Mondays and Thursdays, and every servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except for the person who has enmity and hatred with his brother. It is said: Give them respite until they reconcile."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5030","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The deeds of people are presented twice every week, on Monday and Thursday. Every believing servant is forgiven except for the one who has enmity and hatred with his brother. It is said: Leave both of them until they reconcile."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5031","Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah bin Abi Mu'it (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The person who reconciles between people is not a liar; he speaks good words and conveys good words (to both sides)."" Imam Muslim has narrated this addition: Umm Kulthum (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""I did not hear him—that is, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)—permit lying in any matter except for three things: in war, in reconciling between people, and in conversation between a husband and wife."" Agreed upon."
"5032","And the hadith narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Satan has despaired."" It is mentioned in the chapter of Waswasah. Narrated by Muslim."
"5033","Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Lying is permissible only in three cases: a man lying to please his wife, lying during war, and lying to reconcile between people."" Sahih, narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"5034","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not appropriate for a Muslim to cut off relations with another Muslim for more than three days. When he meets him, he should greet him with salam three times. If each time the other does not respond to the salam, then (the one who offered salam) is absolved of the sin of breaking relations."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5035","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for any Muslim to sever relations with his (Muslim) brother for more than three days. Whoever severs relations for more than three days and dies in that state, he will enter Hell."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood."
"5036","Abu Khirash Salmi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever severs contact with his brother for a whole year, it is as if he has shed his blood."" Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5037","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a believer to shun another believer for more than three days. When three days have passed, he should meet him and greet him with salam. If the other responds to the salam, then both share in the reward; but if he does not respond, then that person bears the sin, while the one who offered salam is absolved from the act of shunning."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5038","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of an act better in rank than fasting, charity, and prayer?"" The narrator states, we said: ""Do tell us."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Reconciling between two parties, friends, or relatives; for discord between two parties is a trait that destroys (good deeds)."" Abu Dawood, Tirmidhi, and Imam Tirmidhi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This hadith is authentic. Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood and Tirmidhi."
"5039","Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The disease of previous nations has crept into you (unnoticed): envy and hatred and enmity, and it is something that destroys good deeds. I am not saying that it shaves the hair, but rather it destroys the religion."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and al-Tirmidhi."
"5040","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Beware of envy, for envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood."" Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5041","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Beware of sowing discord between two (parties, friends, relatives), for it destroys (the religion)."" Its chain is Hasan, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5042","It is narrated from Abu Surmah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever causes harm to a (Muslim), Allah will cause harm to him in return, and whoever puts someone in hardship, Allah will put him in hardship."" Ibn Majah, Tirmidhi, and they said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ibn Majah and Tirmidhi."
"5043","Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: ""Cursed is the person who harms a believer or deceives him."" Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5044","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended the pulpit and proclaimed loudly: ""O people! Those of you who have accepted Islam with your tongues while faith has not yet entered your hearts, do not harm the Muslims, nor disgrace them, nor seek out their faults. For whoever seeks out the faults of his (Muslim) brother, Allah will pursue his faults, and whoever's faults Allah pursues, He will disgrace him even if he is in the midst of his house."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5045","Saeed bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The gravest form of usury is to speak insolently about the honor of a Muslim."" Its chain is authentic, narrated by Abu Dawood and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5046","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When my Lord took me on the Night Journey, I passed by people who had nails of copper with which they were scratching their faces and chests. I said: 'O Jibreel! Who are these people?' He said: 'These are the ones who used to eat the flesh of people (i.e., backbite them) and attack their honor.'"" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5047","Mistawrid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever eats a morsel because of (the backbiting of) a Muslim man, Allah will feed him its like from Hell, and whoever wears a garment because of (the backbiting of) a Muslim man, Allah will clothe him its like from Hell, and whoever stands in a place of fame and show-off, Allah will make him stand in a place of fame and show-off on the Day of Resurrection."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5048","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Good expectation (of Allah) is part of good worship."" Its chain is authentic; narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood."
"5049","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Safiyyah’s (may Allah be pleased with her) camel became ill while Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) had an extra mount. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her): “Give her (Safiyyah) a camel.” She said: “Should I give it to this Jewess!” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) became upset and he refrained from her company for several days during Dhu al-Hijjah, Muharram, and a few days of Safar. Its chain is authentic, narrated by Abu Dawood. And the hadith narrated from Mu’adh bin Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): “Whoever protects the honor of a believer...” has already passed in the chapter of Compassion and Mercy."
"5050","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him) saw a man stealing, so Isa (peace be upon him) said to him: 'You have stolen.' He replied, 'By Him besides whom there is no true deity! I have not.' (Upon this) Isa (peace be upon him) said: 'I believe in Allah, and I deny my own self.'"" Narrated by Muslim."
"5051","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Poverty is close to becoming disbelief (due to objecting to Allah), and envy is close to overpowering destiny."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5052","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever presents an excuse to his (Muslim) brother and he does not consider him excused or does not accept his excuse, then upon him is the sin like that of a tax collector."" Weak, narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman. Both of these narrations have been narrated by Imam Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman, and he said: By ((al-mukas)), the one who takes 'ushr (a type of tax) is meant."
"5053","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A believer is not bitten from the same hole twice."" Agreed upon."
"5054","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Ashajj, the chief of Abdul Qais: ""There are two qualities in you that Allah loves: forbearance and dignity."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5055","It is narrated from Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Forbearance is from Allah, and haste is from Satan.” Imam Tirmidhi narrated this hadith, and he called it ‘gharib’, and some hadith scholars have discussed the memory of this hadith’s narrator, Abdul Muhaymin bin Abbas. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5056","Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only one who slips up is forbearing, and only one with experience is wise."" Ahmad, Tirmidhi, and Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is Hasan Gharib. Hasan, narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"5057","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man requested the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Advise me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Reflect upon the matter; if you see goodness and benefit in its outcome, then proceed with it, and if you fear misguidance, then do not do it."" Its chain is weak, and it is rejected. It is narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"5058","Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrates from his father, while A'mash said: I know this (hadith) only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is better not to act hastily in anything except for deeds of the Hereafter."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5059","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Sarjis (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Good character, forbearance and dignity, and moderation are one twenty-fourth part of Prophethood."" Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi."
"5060","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A good way and good character are one twenty-fifth part of Prophethood."" Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5061","Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""When a man speaks and looks around while talking (to see if anyone else is listening), then it is a trust."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"5062","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Abu Al-Haisham bin Al-Tihan: ""Do you have any servant?"" He replied: No. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When captives come to us, then come to us."" Two slaves were brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, so Abu Al-Haisham also came to him. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Choose any one of them."" He said: O Messenger of Allah! You choose for me. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The one who is consulted is trustworthy. Take this one, for I have seen him performing prayer. I advise you to treat him well."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Tirmidhi."
"5063","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three gatherings—except those in which there is talk of unlawful killing, or adultery, or unlawfully acquiring wealth—are confidential (and what is said in them is a trust)."" Its chain is weak; narrated by Abu Dawood. And the hadith narrated from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) that: ""Indeed, it is a great trust"" has already been mentioned in the first section of the chapter on intimacy."
"5064","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When Allah created the intellect, He said to it: Stand up, so it stood up. Then He said to it: Turn back, so it turned back. Then He said to it: Pay attention to the front, so it came to the front. Then He said to it: Sit down, so it sat down. Then He said: I have made you the best, most superior, and most excellent among all My creation. Because of you I will hold accountable, because of you I will bestow, and because of you I am recognized. Because of you I will punish, and reward and recompense also depend on you."" Some scholars have commented regarding this. Its chain is fabricated. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5065","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person may be among those who perform prayers, observe fasts, give zakat, and perform Hajj and Umrah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned all good deeds in this way. ""But the reward for this person will be given in proportion to his intellect."" Its chain of narration is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5066","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: ""Abu Dharr! There is no intelligence like planning, no piety like refraining from doubtful matters, and no nobility like good character."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5067","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Moderation in spending is half of livelihood, friendship and love with good people is half of wisdom, and asking good questions is half of knowledge."" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all four of these hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is weak and rejected. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5068","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah is gentle, loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness, nor for anything else."" And in another narration of Muslim: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): ""Adopt gentleness, avoid harshness and foul language. Indeed, whenever gentleness is found in something, it adorns it, and whenever it is removed from something, it makes it defective."" Agreed upon."
"5069","Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of all good."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5070","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by an Ansari man who was advising his brother regarding modesty (saying, ""Do not be so shy""). The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Leave him, for modesty is a part of faith."" Agreed upon."
"5071","Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty brings nothing but good."" In another narration: ""Modesty is nothing but goodness in its entirety."" Agreed upon."
"5072","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the sayings that people have obtained from the previous prophets is this: If you feel no shame, then do whatever you wish."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5073","Nawwas bin Sam'an (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) about virtue and sin. He (peace be upon him) said: ""Virtue is good character, while sin is that which troubles your heart and you dislike that people should come to know of it."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5074","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The most beloved of you to me is the one who has the best character among you."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5075","Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one who has the best character among you."" Agreed upon."
"5076","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given his share with gentleness, he has been given his share of goodness in this world and the Hereafter. And whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness, he is deprived of his share of goodness in this world and the Hereafter."" Hasan, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"5077","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Modesty is a part of faith, and the faithful will be in Paradise, while obscenity is evil and the evil ones will be in Hell."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"5078","It is narrated from a man of the Muzainah tribe, who said: The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the best thing that has been given to a person? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Good character."" Sahih, narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5079","And in Sharh al-Sunnah, it is narrated from Usamah bin Sharik. Authentic, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"5080","Haritha bin Wahb (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person with bad character and a hard heart will not enter Paradise."" (Abu Dawood, Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman). And the author of Jami' al-Usul has also narrated it, and in it, it is narrated from Haritha, and likewise, it is narrated from him in Sharh al-Sunnah, and its wording is: He said: ""A boastful and harsh person will not enter Paradise."" The meaning of ""ja'zari"" is said to be: ""harsh-natured and harsh-tongued."" And in the manuscripts of Misbah, it is narrated from Ikrimah bin Wahb, and its wording is: The meaning of ""jawwaz"" is: a miser who hoards wealth, and the meaning of ""ja'zari"" is: ""harsh-natured and harsh-tongued."" Sahih, narrated by Abu Dawood and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman and in Sharh al-Sunnah and mentioned in Misbah al-Sunnah."
"5081","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, nothing will be placed in the believer’s scale heavier than good character, and Allah certainly does not like the one who is foul-mouthed and engages in obscene talk."" (Tirmidhi), and he said: This hadith is Hasan Sahih, and Abu Dawood has narrated the first part. Its chain is authentic, narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"5082","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, a believer, because of his good character, attains the rank of one who fasts and stands (in prayer) at night."" Hasan, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5083","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: ""Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good one—it will erase it, and deal with people with good character."" Hasan, narrated by Ahmad, al-Tirmidhi, and al-Darimi."
"5084","Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Shall I not inform you about those people upon whom the Fire of Hell is forbidden, or who are forbidden for the Fire of Hell? They are those who are easy-going, gentle, approachable, and soft-natured.” Ahmad, Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is Hasan Gharib. Its chain is Hasan, narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"5085","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A believer is simple-hearted and generous, while a wicked person is deceitful and miserly."" Its chain is weak; narrated by Ahmad, al-Tirmidhi, and Abu Dawood."
"5086","Makhool narrates: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A believer is gentle in temperament and dignified, like a camel with a nose-ring; when it is led, it follows, and when it is made to sit on a rock, it sits."" Imam Tirmidhi narrated it as a mursal narration. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Tirmidhi."
"5087","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""A Muslim who mixes with people and is patient over their harm is better than the one who does not mix with people and is not patient over their harm."" Sahih, narrated by Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."
"5088","Sahl bin Mu’adh narrates from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever controls his anger while he is able to act upon it, Allah will call him before all of creation on the Day of Resurrection and will let him choose whichever hur (maiden) he wishes.” Tirmidhi, Abu Dawood. And Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is hasan. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Abu Dawood."
"5089","And in the narration of Abu Dawood, Suwaid bin Wahb narrated from a man among the children of the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him), who narrated from his father, he said: ""Allah will fill his heart with peace and faith."" And the hadith narrated from Suwaid: ""Whoever gives up wearing beautiful clothes,"" is mentioned in the Book of Clothing. Its chain is weak, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5090","Zaid bin Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every religion has some distinguishing characteristics, and the distinguishing characteristic of Islam is modesty."" Imam Malik has narrated it as a mursal narration. Its chain is weak, narrated by Malik."
"5091","Ibn Majah and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman narrated from Anas and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them. Weak, narrated by Ibn Majah and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5092","Ibn Majah and Bayhaqi have narrated it from Anas and Ibn Abbas in Shub al-Iman. Weak, narrated by Ibn Majah and Al-Bayhaqi in Shab al-Iman."
"5093","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, modesty and faith go together; when one of them is taken away, the other is also taken away."" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5094","And in the narration of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, it is stated: ""When one of them is deprived, the other also follows after it."" Its chain of narration is weak, even fabricated. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5095","Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When I placed my foot in the stirrup, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me his final advice, saying: ""Mu'adh! Treat people with good manners."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Malik."
"5096","Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: It has reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent to perfect good character."" Chain is weak, narrated by Malik."
"5097","Imam Ahmad narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him). Its chain is weak, narrated by Ahmad."
"5098","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, looked into the mirror, he would recite this supplication: ""All praise is due to Allah who has made my appearance and character good, and who has adorned me by protecting me from the faults that were in others."" Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman, it is a mursal narration. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5099","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! You have created me well, so beautify my character as well."" Its chain is authentic, narrated by Ahmad."
"5100","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the best among you?"" They said, ""Please do tell us."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you are those whose lives are the longest among you and whose character is the best among you."" Hasan, narrated by Ahmad."
"5101","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most complete in faith among the believers are those who have the best character among them."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Al-Darimi."
"5102","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man abused Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, while the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was sitting there. He was amazed and smiling. When the man became more insolent, Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, replied to one of his remarks, at which the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, became angry and stood up. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, went to him and said: O Messenger of Allah! He kept abusing me while you were sitting there, but when I replied to one of his remarks, you became angry and stood up. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There was an angel with you who was replying to him, but when you replied, Satan appeared."" Then he said: ""O Abu Bakr! Three things are absolutely true: Whoever is wronged and overlooks it for the sake of Allah, Allah the Exalted grants him strength and victory in return; whoever gives in order to maintain ties of kinship, Allah gives him more in return; and whoever asks (begs) in order to increase his wealth, Allah only increases him in poverty."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Ahmad."
"5103","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for the people of a household, He grants them gentleness, and when He deprives a household of it, He causes them loss because of it."" Sahih, narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5104","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man requested the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""Advise me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not get angry."" He requested this several times, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (each time) said: ""Do not get angry."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5105","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A strong person is not the one who overpowers others in wrestling; rather, a strong person is the one who controls himself at the time of anger."" Agreed upon."
"5106","Haritha bin Wahb (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not inform you about the people of Paradise? Every weak person whom people consider weak and powerless, but if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it for him. Shall I not inform you about the people of Hell? Every harsh, miserly, and arrogant person."" And in the narration of Muslim: ""Every miserly, mean, and arrogant person."" Agreed upon."
"5107","Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever has faith equal to a mustard seed in his heart will not enter Hell, and whoever has arrogance equal to a mustard seed in his heart will not enter Paradise."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5108","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has even a mustard seed's weight of arrogance in his heart will not enter Paradise."" A man asked, ""A person likes that his clothes and shoes are good. (Is this also arrogance?)"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Indeed, Allah is beautiful and loves beauty. Arrogance means rejecting the truth and looking down on people."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5109","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three types of people with whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them."" In another narration: ""Nor will He look at them with mercy, and for them is a painful punishment: an old adulterer, a lying king, and an arrogant poor person."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5110","Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah Almighty says: Grandeur is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment; whoever competes with Me regarding either of them, I will admit him into the Fire."" In another narration: ""I will throw him into the Fire."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5111","Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “A man continues to consider himself great until he is written among the arrogant and the oppressors, and thus he will be afflicted with the same (punishment) with which they were afflicted.” Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5112","Amr bin Shu’aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that they narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: “The arrogant will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection in the form of tiny ants in the shape of men. Humiliation will cover them from every place. They will be driven to a prison in Hell called ‘Boulas’. The hottest fire will envelop them, and they will be given to drink the pus of the inhabitants of Hell, called ‘Teenat al-Khabal’.” Hasan, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5113","Atiyyah bin Urwah Sa'di narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Anger is from Satan, and Satan was created from fire, and fire is extinguished only with water. So when one of you becomes angry, he should perform ablution."" Its chain is good. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5114","It is narrated from Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you becomes angry while standing, he should sit down. If the anger leaves him, well and good; otherwise, he should lie down."" Sahih, narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"5115","Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Wretched is the servant who shows arrogance and forgets the Most High and Exalted (Allah), wretched is the servant who commits oppression and excess and forgets the Dominant and Supreme Being, wretched is the servant who forgets, remains engrossed in play and amusement, and forgets the graves and his own decay, wretched is the servant who shows arrogance and rebellion and forgets his beginning and end, wretched is the servant who seeks the world in exchange for religion, wretched is the servant who corrupts the religion through doubts, the worst is the servant whom greed and avarice drag away, wretched is the servant whom desire leads astray, wretched is the servant whom the desire for the world humiliates."" Tirmidhi, Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman, both said: Its chain is not strong, and Imam Tirmidhi also said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak, narrated by Tirmidhi and Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5116","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The servant who swallows a gulp of anger for the sake of Allah Almighty, that gulp is the best in the sight of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Ahmad."
"5117","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) explained Allah Almighty’s statement (Repel [evil] with that which is best) as follows: To be patient at the time of anger, to forgive when a mistake is made; when they do so, Allah will protect them and their enemies will be humbled, as if he is a close, intimate friend. Imam Bukhari narrated this in a suspended form. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bukhari in Tafsir (Chapter 4 before Hadith 4816, suspended without chain)."
"5118","Bahz bin Hakim narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Anger spoils faith just as aloes spoil honey."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5119","It is narrated from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said on the pulpit: O people! Adopt humility, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever adopts humility for the sake of Allah, Allah grants him elevation; he considers himself small in his own eyes, but in the eyes of people he is great. And whoever is arrogant, Allah makes him low; he is small in the eyes of people while he considers himself great, until he becomes, in their view, more despicable and contemptible than a dog or a pig."" Its chain is fabricated. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5120","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Musa bin Imran (peace be upon him) asked: 'O Lord! Which of Your servants is the most honorable in Your sight?' He said: 'The one who forgives despite having the power (to take revenge).'""Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5121","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever guards his tongue, Allah will conceal his faults; whoever restrains his anger, on the Day of Resurrection Allah will withhold His punishment from him; and whoever apologizes before Allah, Allah will accept his apology."" Its chain of narration is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5122","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things are causes of salvation and three things are causes of destruction. The things that cause salvation are: adopting the fear of Allah both outwardly and inwardly, speaking the truth in pleasure and displeasure, and adopting moderation in wealth and poverty. And the things that cause destruction are: following such desires that are obeyed, such miserliness that is followed, and a person's self-admiration, and this is the most destructive of all."" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all five hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5123","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Oppression will be the cause of many darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."" Agreed upon."
"5124","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah gives respite to the oppressor, but when He seizes him, He does not let him go."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""Such is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are doing wrong."" Agreed upon."
"5125","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by the place of Hijr, he said: ""Enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves weeping, lest you be afflicted with the same punishment that befell them."" Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, covered his head and hastened his pace until he had passed through the valley. Agreed upon."
"5126","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has wronged his (Muslim) brother with regard to his honor or anything else, let him seek forgiveness from him (in this world) before a day comes when there will be no dinar or dirham. If he has good deeds, they will be taken from him in proportion to his wrongdoing, and if he has no good deeds, the sins of the wronged person will be placed upon him."" Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5127","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do you know who is the bankrupt?"" They replied, the one who has neither dirham nor wealth and possessions. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The bankrupt of my Ummah is the one who will come on the Day of Resurrection with prayers, fasting, and zakat, but he will also come having abused someone, slandered someone, unlawfully consumed the wealth of someone, shed the blood of someone, and beaten someone. So his good deeds will be given to those (whom he wronged), and if his good deeds run out before the rights are fulfilled, then their sins will be placed upon him, and he will be thrown into the Hellfire."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5128","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, you will certainly pay the rights to those entitled to them, until even the horned goat will be recompensed for the hornless goat."" Narrated by Muslim. And the hadith narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Beware of oppression."" is mentioned in the chapter of spending."
"5129","Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not be an imitator, (such that) you say: If people do good, we will also do good, and if they do wrong, we will also do wrong. Rather, resolve within yourselves that if people do good, you will also do good, and if they do evil, you will not do injustice."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5130","It is narrated from Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he wrote a letter to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) asking her to write him a concise advice. So she wrote: Peace be upon you! To proceed! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever seeks the pleasure of Allah at the cost of people's displeasure, Allah will suffice him against the evil of the people; and whoever seeks the pleasure of people at the cost of Allah's displeasure, Allah will leave him to the people."" And peace be upon you! Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5131","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When this verse was revealed: ""Those who believe and do not mix their faith with injustice,"" this was hard on the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and they said: O Messenger of Allah! Who among us has not wronged himself? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It does not mean that; rather, it means shirk (associating partners with Allah). Have you not heard the saying of Luqman to his son: 'O my son! Do not associate anything with Allah, for indeed shirk is a great injustice.'"" In another narration: ""It is not as you think; it is as Luqman said to his son."" Agreed upon."
"5132","It is narrated from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the worst person in status will be the one who ruined his Hereafter for the sake of someone else's worldly life."" Its chain is weak, narrated by Ibn Majah."
"5133","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three types of record of deeds. One is the record of deeds which Allah will not forgive, and that is associating partners with Allah. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: 'Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him.' The second is the record of deeds which Allah will not leave alone, and that is the wrongs committed by people against each other, until they settle the matter among themselves. And the third is the record of deeds which Allah does not care about, and that is the wrongs committed by people between themselves and Allah; this is up to Allah—if He wills, He will punish, and if He wills, He will pardon."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5134","Ali narrates, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for he asks Allah for his right, and indeed Allah does not withhold the right from its owner."" Its chain of narration is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5135","It is narrated from Aws bin Sharhabil (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever accompanies an oppressor in order to strengthen him, while he knows that he is an oppressor, such a person goes out of Islam."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5136","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard a man saying that a wrongdoer only harms himself. Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Yes, by Allah! Even the hoopoe bird becomes weak and dies in its nest because of the oppression of the oppressor. Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all four hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5137","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand; if he is not able to do so, then with his tongue; and if he is not able to do that, then with his heart (by planning to change it and by hating it), and that is the weakest level of faith."" Narrated by Muslim."
"5138","Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The example of the one who is lax in enforcing the limits set by Allah and the one who falls into them is like a people who drew lots for places in a boat. Some of them were in its lower deck and some in its upper deck. Those who were in the lower deck, when they needed water, would have to pass by those above them, which caused discomfort to the upper deck people. So the people in the lower deck took an axe and began to make a hole in the bottom of the boat. The people above came to them and asked: ‘What are you doing?’ They replied: ‘You are troubled when we pass above you, and we need water as well.’ If the people above stop their hands, they will save both themselves and the others; but if they leave them to what they want, they will destroy both themselves and the others.” Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5139","Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, a man will be brought and thrown into Hell. His intestines will come out in the fire, and he will circle around them as a donkey circles around a millstone. The people of Hell will gather around him and ask: O so-and-so! What has happened to you? Did you not command us to do good and forbid us from evil? He will say: I used to command you to do good but did not do it myself, and I used to forbid you from evil but committed it myself."" Agreed upon."
"5140","It is narrated from Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! You must certainly enjoin good and forbid evil, otherwise it is near that Allah will send His punishment upon you, then you will supplicate to Him but He will not accept your supplications."" Hasan, narrated by Tirmidhi."
"5141","Urs bin Umairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a sin is committed on the earth and a person present there dislikes it, then he is like one who is not present there. And the one who is not present there but is pleased with it, then he is like one who is present there."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5142","It is narrated from Abu Bakr Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: ""O people! You recite this verse: 'O you who believe! Take care of your own selves. If you are guided, no one who goes astray can harm you.' I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: 'Indeed, when people see an evil and do not stop it, then it is near that Allah will encompass them all with His punishment.'"" (Ibn Majah, Tirmidhi, and Imam Tirmidhi declared it authentic.) And in the narration of Abu Dawood: ""When they see the oppressor (committing oppression) and do not restrain his hands, then it is near that Allah will encompass them all with punishment."" And in another narration of Abu Dawood: ""Any nation in which sins are committed, and they do not stop them despite having the power to do so, then it is near that Allah will encompass them all with punishment."" In another narration: ""If a minority of a nation becomes involved in sin, and the majority, though not committing the sin themselves, do not stop those who do, (then they too will be afflicted with punishment)."" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Ibn Majah, Tirmidhi, and Abu Dawood."
"5143","Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""If a person commits a sin among a people and they do not stop him despite having the power to do so, then before they die, Allah will afflict them all with His punishment."" Chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Dawood and Ibn Majah."
"5144","Regarding the statement of Allah Almighty: ""Hold fast to your own selves; when you are rightly guided, those who go astray cannot harm you,"" Abu Tha’labah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: He said, Listen! By Allah, I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about this, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rather, you must continue to enjoin good and forbid evil, until you see that miserliness is obeyed, desires are followed, the world is preferred, and every person is pleased with his own opinion and intellect, and you see an affair which it is difficult to avoid, then hold fast to your own selves and leave the common people to their affairs, for ahead are coming the days of patience. Whoever is patient in those days will be like one who holds a burning ember, and for the one who acts in those days, there will be the reward of fifty men doing the same deed."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! The reward of fifty men among them?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""The reward of fifty men among you."" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."
"5145","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to deliver a sermon to us after the Asr prayer, and he mentioned all the events that would occur until the Day of Resurrection. Some people remembered it, and some forgot it. Among what he said in his address was: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The world is sweet and lush. Indeed, Allah is going to make you successors in it, so He will see how you act. Beware! Be cautious of the world, and be cautious of (the temptation of) women."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned: ""On the Day of Resurrection, for every betrayer, there will be a flag according to the extent of his betrayal in the world, and there is no betrayal greater than the betrayal of the general leader (the head of state); his flag will be fixed on his buttocks. And the fear of people should not prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he knows it."" In another narration: ""If he sees an evil, he should stop it, and the fear of people should not prevent him from doing so."" Thus (after narrating this), Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep and said: ""Indeed, we saw this, but the fear of people prevented us from speaking about it."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Listen! The children of Adam were created in different categories: among them, some were created as believers, they lived as such and died as such; and among them, some were created as disbelievers, they lived as such and died as such; and among them, some are born as believers, live as believers, and die as disbelievers; and among them, some are born as disbelievers, live as such, and die as believers."" And the narrator states: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned anger: ""Among them, some get angry quickly and it subsides quickly; one trait is the substitute for the other. And among them, some get angry slowly and it subsides slowly; this too is one trait for another. The best among you is the one who gets angry slowly and it subsides quickly, and the worst among you is the one who gets angry quickly and it subsides slowly."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of anger, for it is a burning coal on the heart of the son of Adam. Do you not see the swelling of his veins and the redness of his eyes? Whoever feels such a state should lie down and attach himself to the ground."" The narrator states: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned debt and said: ""Some of you are good in repayment, but when they have to take a loan, they are harsh in collection; this trait is the substitute for the other (however, this quality is not praiseworthy). Some are bad in repayment but good in collection; this too is the substitute for the other (however, this quality is not praiseworthy). The best among you is the one who, when he owes a debt, repays it well, and when he has to collect a debt, he is gentle in collection. The worst among you is the one who is bad in repayment and harsh in collection."" Until, when the sunlight reached the tops of the date palms and the sides of the walls, he said: ""Listen! Only as much of the world remains as the portion of this day that remains."" Chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5146","Abu Bakhtari narrates from a companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will not be destroyed due to sins until they begin to present false excuses to justify their sins."" Its chain is authentic, narrated by Abu Dawood."
"5147","Adi bin Adi Kindi narrates: Our freed slave narrated to us that he heard my grandfather saying that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Indeed, Allah does not punish all people because of the disobedience of some among them, until they see evil before them and, while having the power to stop it, do not do so. When they become like this, then Allah subjects all—both the general and the specific (the many and the few)—to punishment."" Hasan, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"5148","Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When the Children of Israel became involved in sins, their scholars forbade them, but when they did not desist, the scholars began to sit with them and eat and drink with them. Allah made their hearts resemble one another, and cursed them on the tongue of Dawud and ‘Isa son of Maryam, and this happened because they disobeyed and transgressed.” The narrator says, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was reclining, then he sat up and said: “No (you will not succeed either), by the One in Whose hand is my soul! Until you strictly prevent them (the sinners, the wrongdoers).” And in the narration of Abu Dawud, he said: “Never, by Allah! You must certainly enjoin good, you must certainly forbid evil, you must certainly seize the hand of the wrongdoer, you must certainly incline him towards the truth, and you must certainly keep him established upon the truth, otherwise Allah will make your hearts resemble one another, then He will curse you as He cursed them.” Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawud."
"5149","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night of Mi'raj, I saw some men whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: 'O Jibreel! Who are these people?' He replied: 'These are the preachers of your ummah; they used to enjoin righteousness upon people but forgot themselves.'""In Sharh al-Sunnah, al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman, and in their narration, it is mentioned: ""They are the preachers of your ummah who used to say but did not do; they used to recite the Book of Allah but did not act upon it.""Hasan. Narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5150","Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A tablecloth consisting of bread and meat was sent down from the sky, and they were commanded not to be treacherous and not to store anything for the next day, but they committed treachery, stored it, and kept it for the next day, because of which they were transformed into monkeys and pigs."" Its chain is weak, narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5151","Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last era, my Ummah will face trials and tribulations from their rulers, and only that person will be saved who, recognizing Allah's religion, strives against it with his tongue, his hand, and his heart. He is the one who will attain the first blessings. And the person who has recognized Allah's religion and affirmed it, and the man who recognized Allah's religion but remained silent about its (explanation and details)—if he saw someone doing a good deed, he liked it, and if he saw someone doing a bad deed, he was displeased with it. This person succeeded through his hidden likes and dislikes."" Its chain is weak; it is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5152","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed to Jibreel (peace be upon him) to overturn such-and-such city along with its inhabitants. He said: 'My Lord! Among them is Your such-and-such servant who has not disobeyed You even for the blink of an eye.' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Allah, the Exalted, said: Overturn it upon him and upon them, for his face never changed for My sake even for a moment.'"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5153","Abu Saeed (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will ask the servant on the Day of Resurrection: What happened to you that when you saw evil, you did not stop it?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He will be taught his argument and he will say: O my Lord! I feared the people and hoped in You."" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all three hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5154","Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, virtue and evil are two (distinct) creations. On the Day of Resurrection, they will be made to stand before the people. Thus, virtue will give glad tidings to its companions (i.e., the righteous) and promise them good, while evil will say: 'Stay away, stay away,' but those (who committed evil) will not be able to separate themselves from it."" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
